WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.730
- [Zac] Michael Audrey Myers
was born in the year 1957,

00:00:02.730 --> 00:00:04.090
as the second child in his family

00:00:04.090 --> 00:00:05.630
after his nine year old sister, Judith.

00:00:05.630 --> 00:00:07.180
In this video, I'm only analyzing

00:00:07.180 --> 00:00:08.910
the original timeline of Michael's life,

00:00:08.910 --> 00:00:11.350
which includes the events
of Halloween, Halloween II,

00:00:11.350 --> 00:00:13.110
Return, Revenge and Curse.

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:14.510
The date of Michael's
birth in this timeline

00:00:14.510 --> 00:00:16.990
is not explicitly stated, but
in Halloween Resurrection,

00:00:16.990 --> 00:00:20.200
which is part of a different
timeline, we learn this...

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:21.613
- Michael Myers.

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:26.810
Born October 19th, 1957.

00:00:26.810 --> 00:00:27.700
- [Zac] Both of these timelines

00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:28.660
start with the same movie,

00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:30.990
Halloween, which would imply
that Michael was also born

00:00:30.990 --> 00:00:32.850
on October 19th in that movie.

00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:34.280
I like to think about
the Halloween timeline

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:36.800
as a train map, which I
call the Halloween Express.

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:38.090
So think about it like this.

00:00:38.090 --> 00:00:39.940
If we depart from the
station, Halloween 1,

00:00:39.940 --> 00:00:42.150
at exactly 10:19, we can go straight,

00:00:42.150 --> 00:00:43.700
and end up in Curse of Michael Myers,

00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:46.560
or we can go this way, and end
up at Halloween Resurrection.

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:47.810
No matter which way we went,

00:00:47.810 --> 00:00:50.900
we still departed from the
Halloween 1 station at 10:19.

00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:52.790
The counter-argument to that
idea is Halloween (2018).

00:00:52.790 --> 00:00:55.230
In Rick Rosenthal's Halloween II,

00:00:55.230 --> 00:00:57.330
we learn Michael Myers and
Laurie Strode are siblings,

00:00:57.330 --> 00:00:59.030
which would mean that
they were always siblings,

00:00:59.030 --> 00:01:00.250
even in Halloween 1.

00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:01.920
However, in Halloween (2018),

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:03.050
they don't appear to be related,

00:01:03.050 --> 00:01:03.931
because the 40-year timeline

00:01:03.931 --> 00:01:06.060
does not pass through Halloween II.

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:08.100
However, it's possible that
they still are related,

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:09.640
just nobody ever finds out.

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:11.170
- Wasn't it her brother

00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:13.970
who like cold blooded
murderated all those teenagers?

00:01:13.970 --> 00:01:16.680
- No. That's just a myth
that some people made up

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:17.960
to make him feel better I think.

00:01:17.960 --> 00:01:19.140
- There are other retcons

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:20.610
that don't carry over to other timelines,

00:01:20.610 --> 00:01:21.780
so all I'll say with certainty

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:24.920
is that Michael was born
sometime in the year 1957.

00:01:24.920 --> 00:01:25.837
Yeah, this is gonna be

00:01:25.837 --> 00:01:28.080
one of *those* episodes of Horror History.

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:30.220
Michael was three years old
when his sister Laurie was born

00:01:30.220 --> 00:01:31.730
in February 1961.

00:01:31.730 --> 00:01:33.233
His early childhood is
presumably a normal one,

00:01:33.233 --> 00:01:35.120
until two and a half years later,

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:37.950
when he is cursed by an
ancient demon known as Thorn.

00:01:37.950 --> 00:01:39.500
To learn what really happened to Michael

00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:41.070
after disappearing from Haddonfield,

00:01:41.070 --> 00:01:43.024
stick around to the end of this video.

00:01:43.024 --> 00:01:45.607
(upbeat music)

00:01:49.370 --> 00:01:50.600
Welcome to Horror History,

00:01:50.600 --> 00:01:52.640
and welcome aboard the Halloween Express.

00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:53.530
The Halloween Timeline

00:01:53.530 --> 00:01:55.540
can be a little bit confusing at times.

00:01:55.540 --> 00:01:56.910
We've got many different continuities

00:01:56.910 --> 00:01:58.480
branching out from the first two movies.

00:01:58.480 --> 00:02:00.720
Then we've got a reboot, which
isn't connected to anything

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:02.420
and Halloween III, a separate world

00:02:02.420 --> 00:02:04.490
where the original
Halloween is just a movie.

00:02:04.490 --> 00:02:06.410
On top of that there are comics and novels

00:02:06.410 --> 00:02:08.810
whose status in the canon
can be kind of unclear.

00:02:08.810 --> 00:02:10.450
So to make things easy, for this episode,

00:02:10.450 --> 00:02:12.580
we're gonna be traveling
right down the original route,

00:02:12.580 --> 00:02:15.010
as we analyze horror's
most iconic slasher.

00:02:15.010 --> 00:02:17.470
Michael Myers was named after
a real life Michael Myers

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:19.140
by the original director, John Carpenter,

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:20.830
who wanted to honor the
European distributor

00:02:20.830 --> 00:02:23.210
of his previous film,
Assault on Precinct 13.

00:02:23.210 --> 00:02:25.300
To understand how Michael
became the soulless,

00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:26.510
immortal killer that he is,

00:02:26.510 --> 00:02:30.433
we've gotta take it way
back to about 500 BCE.

00:02:30.433 --> 00:02:32.850
(soft music)

00:02:35.560 --> 00:02:38.180
The Myers family is descended
from an ancient Druid tribe

00:02:38.180 --> 00:02:40.340
who worshiped great astronomical deities.

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:42.140
The Druids were a mysterious Celtic order

00:02:42.140 --> 00:02:43.960
known for their studies
of religious scriptures,

00:02:43.960 --> 00:02:46.140
philosophy, astronomy, and divine lore.

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:47.470
They were said to make sacrifices,

00:02:47.470 --> 00:02:49.360
which sometimes included human sacrifices

00:02:49.360 --> 00:02:50.280
for the sick or injured,

00:02:50.280 --> 00:02:51.630
which allegedly included the burning

00:02:51.630 --> 00:02:53.740
of huge wickerwork
figures filled with men.

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:55.510
Not much is known of Druid culture,

00:02:55.510 --> 00:02:57.120
because they did not keep any records,

00:02:57.120 --> 00:03:00.650
but around 500 BCE they did
create an ancient alphabet

00:03:00.650 --> 00:03:02.410
carved into stone and wood ruins.

00:03:02.410 --> 00:03:04.190
These ruins were used for Pagan rituals

00:03:04.190 --> 00:03:06.450
in order to help the tribe
predict future events.

00:03:06.450 --> 00:03:08.280
One of the icons was the symbol of Thorn,

00:03:08.280 --> 00:03:10.160
which was designed after
the Thorn constellation

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:11.910
and was used to represent an ancient demon

00:03:11.910 --> 00:03:13.460
that plagued the Celtic people.

00:03:15.490 --> 00:03:16.630
- [Tommy] Among the ancient Druids,

00:03:16.630 --> 00:03:20.060
Thorn represented a demon
that spread sickness,

00:03:20.060 --> 00:03:21.960
destroyed crops,

00:03:21.960 --> 00:03:24.800
brought death to hundreds
of thousands of people.

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:25.910
According to Celtic legend,

00:03:25.910 --> 00:03:29.640
one child from each tribe
was chosen to be inflicted

00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:30.980
with the Curse of Thorn.

00:03:30.980 --> 00:03:33.230
- While knowledge of the
demon Thorn faded into legend

00:03:33.230 --> 00:03:34.250
over the coming millenia,

00:03:34.250 --> 00:03:36.010
the bloodline of the tribe stayed intact,

00:03:36.010 --> 00:03:37.500
and one offshoot of the population

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:39.527
ended up in the Midwest
region of the United States.

00:03:39.527 --> 00:03:42.090
They continued to practice
their ritualistic sacrifices

00:03:42.090 --> 00:03:43.690
in fear of the malicious demon,

00:03:43.690 --> 00:03:45.680
and they called themselves
The Cult of Thorn.

00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:46.970
In the early 1960s,

00:03:46.970 --> 00:03:48.160
the leader of the cult was a man

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:49.330
by the name of Terence Wynn,

00:03:49.330 --> 00:03:51.850
who worked at a sanitarium
known as Smith's Grove by day

00:03:51.850 --> 00:03:53.430
and used the facility as a meeting place

00:03:53.430 --> 00:03:54.666
and a worship ground by night.

00:03:54.666 --> 00:03:58.790
- One child from each tribe
was chosen to be inflicted

00:03:58.790 --> 00:03:59.930
with The Curse of Thorn.

00:03:59.930 --> 00:04:02.490
To offer the blood
sacrifices of its next of kin

00:04:02.490 --> 00:04:03.860
on the night of Samhain.

00:04:03.860 --> 00:04:04.693
- Halloween.

00:04:04.693 --> 00:04:06.360
- The sacrifice of one family

00:04:06.360 --> 00:04:09.280
meant sparing the lives
of an entire tribe.

00:04:09.280 --> 00:04:10.340
- So Dr. Wynn believed

00:04:10.340 --> 00:04:12.180
that if he and his cult
placed The Curse of Thorn

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:13.020
on one child,

00:04:13.020 --> 00:04:15.230
the child would be compelled
to kill his entire family,

00:04:15.230 --> 00:04:16.940
but the rest of the
tribe would be protected

00:04:16.940 --> 00:04:19.570
from things like disease,
death, plague and drought

00:04:19.570 --> 00:04:20.860
for an entire generation.

00:04:20.860 --> 00:04:23.140
I do not know how their
selection process went,

00:04:23.140 --> 00:04:25.410
but Dr. Wynn ends up
choosing a 6-year old boy

00:04:25.410 --> 00:04:26.925
by the name of Michael Audrey Myers.

00:04:26.925 --> 00:04:29.513
The curse must be placed
during the Festival of Samhain.

00:04:29.513 --> 00:04:30.710
- [Loomis] Sam Hain.

00:04:30.710 --> 00:04:32.790
- Which is a Gaelic
festival of Pagan origins

00:04:32.790 --> 00:04:34.410
where the barrier would supposedly be down

00:04:34.410 --> 00:04:36.910
between the real and the
unreal, allowing sacrifices,

00:04:36.910 --> 00:04:38.500
be those crops, animals,

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:41.020
or in the case of the Halloween
movies human sacrifices,

00:04:41.020 --> 00:04:41.853
to be made.

00:04:41.853 --> 00:04:43.030
Samhain takes place every year

00:04:43.030 --> 00:04:44.400
at the end of the harvest season.

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:45.830
Today, in the northern hemisphere,

00:04:45.830 --> 00:04:47.170
we call that Halloween night.

00:04:47.170 --> 00:04:48.590
However, in the eyes of the cult,

00:04:48.590 --> 00:04:51.140
some Halloween nights were
more special than others.

00:04:51.140 --> 00:04:54.410
- [Tommy] The Druids were also great
mathematicians and astronomers.

00:04:54.410 --> 00:04:56.770
The thorn symbol is actually
a constellation of stars

00:04:56.770 --> 00:04:59.620
that appears from time to
time on Halloween night.

00:04:59.620 --> 00:05:01.310
Whenever it appears, he appears.

00:05:01.310 --> 00:05:03.490
- I'd like to note that
the Druids, the Pagans,

00:05:03.490 --> 00:05:04.820
The Festival of Samhain...

00:05:04.820 --> 00:05:05.710
- [Loomis] Sam Hain.

00:05:05.710 --> 00:05:07.990
- And the ritualistic
sacrifice of crops and animals

00:05:07.990 --> 00:05:09.810
during the festival
are based on real life,

00:05:09.810 --> 00:05:12.360
while the Cult of Thorn and the
Thorn constellation are not,

00:05:12.360 --> 00:05:14.210
but the name Thorn is
based off of a letter

00:05:14.210 --> 00:05:15.480
in the old English alphabet.

00:05:15.480 --> 00:05:17.430
It looks kind of like a
"p" and a "b" put together

00:05:17.430 --> 00:05:18.500
so they made the movie version

00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:20.320
just look a little bit more thorny.

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:22.250
The thorn constellation
in the Halloween movies

00:05:22.250 --> 00:05:24.540
appears in the sky at
seemingly random intervals.

00:05:24.540 --> 00:05:25.530
They're just the same years

00:05:25.530 --> 00:05:27.160
that the Halloween movies come out.

00:05:27.160 --> 00:05:30.150
It's first appearance in
Michael's lifetime comes in 1963

00:05:30.150 --> 00:05:32.110
and this is the night
that Dr. Wynn and his cult

00:05:32.110 --> 00:05:33.390
placed the curse on the young boy,

00:05:33.390 --> 00:05:34.730
forever changing his behavior

00:05:34.730 --> 00:05:37.160
and making him an empty,
soulless killing machine.

00:05:37.160 --> 00:05:39.820
In my Things You Missed
episode on Halloween (1978),

00:05:39.820 --> 00:05:41.570
I talked about how
Michael's actions that night

00:05:41.570 --> 00:05:43.130
could be interpreted as representing

00:05:43.130 --> 00:05:44.750
a release of psychosexual trauma

00:05:44.750 --> 00:05:46.600
that Michael was too young to understand.

00:05:46.600 --> 00:05:48.890
I went in depth with the
psychological interpretation

00:05:48.890 --> 00:05:49.723
on that video,

00:05:49.723 --> 00:05:50.760
because it doesn't fall in line

00:05:50.760 --> 00:05:52.710
with the information
presented in Halloween 6,

00:05:52.710 --> 00:05:53.840
The Curse of Michael Myers.

00:05:53.840 --> 00:05:56.428
So in this video, since we're
analyzing the entire character

00:05:56.428 --> 00:05:59.270
that psychological interpretation
doesn't make sense.

00:05:59.270 --> 00:06:01.210
Michael is simply possessed by the cult.

00:06:01.210 --> 00:06:03.380
Michael Myers' power is
described by Dr. Wynn

00:06:03.380 --> 00:06:06.310
as something greater than a
man driven to commit crimes.

00:06:06.310 --> 00:06:07.810
- Evil.

00:06:07.810 --> 00:06:09.390
Pure,

00:06:09.390 --> 00:06:10.283
uncorrupted,

00:06:11.528 --> 00:06:12.750
ancient.

00:06:12.750 --> 00:06:14.770
- [Zac] On October 31st, 1963,

00:06:14.770 --> 00:06:16.310
Michael's parents go out for the evening,

00:06:16.310 --> 00:06:18.330
and his older sister is
hanging out with her boyfriend,

00:06:18.330 --> 00:06:19.980
so he's left in the care of an older woman

00:06:19.980 --> 00:06:21.960
named Mrs. Blankenship across the street.

00:06:21.960 --> 00:06:23.610
He begins to hear a voice in his head.

00:06:23.610 --> 00:06:25.620
Presumably, this was
the voice of Dr. Wynn,

00:06:25.620 --> 00:06:27.990
or possibly the demon Thorn itself.

00:06:27.990 --> 00:06:29.640
- Michael heard a voice?

00:06:29.640 --> 00:06:32.510
- It told him to kill his family.

00:06:32.510 --> 00:06:34.700
- And that's exactly what he does.

00:06:34.700 --> 00:06:36.550
He grabs a knife and goes
to take out his sister

00:06:36.550 --> 00:06:38.010
by stabbing her several times,

00:06:38.010 --> 00:06:39.580
before his parents eventually come home

00:06:39.580 --> 00:06:41.000
to discover what he had done.

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:43.060
Michael is sentenced to
Smith's Grove Sanitarium

00:06:43.060 --> 00:06:45.180
and assigned to a doctor
named Samuel Loomis.

00:06:45.180 --> 00:06:47.657
In a hearing six months
later, in April 1964,

00:06:47.657 --> 00:06:50.140
Loomis was instructed to
report on Michael's progress

00:06:50.140 --> 00:06:51.640
to the court two times a year.

00:06:53.840 --> 00:06:57.570
- Further, Michael Audrey Myers
shall be brought before the court

00:06:57.570 --> 00:06:59.960
on the day of his 21st birthday,

00:06:59.960 --> 00:07:02.470
where he shall be tried as an adult.

00:07:02.470 --> 00:07:04.530
- Michael was seemingly
in a catatonic state,

00:07:04.530 --> 00:07:06.620
causing nearly everyone
to see him as harmless

00:07:06.620 --> 00:07:07.900
other than Dr. Loomis.

00:07:07.900 --> 00:07:10.210
His initial stay at Smith's
Grove lasted 15 years,

00:07:10.210 --> 00:07:12.280
none of which is documented
in the Halloween films.

00:07:12.280 --> 00:07:14.760
However, the non-canon
Chaos Comics material

00:07:14.760 --> 00:07:17.050
tells of Michael's
involvement in more murders.

00:07:17.050 --> 00:07:19.400
These stories occasionally
contradict the canon,

00:07:19.400 --> 00:07:20.840
but they were written to go in tandem

00:07:20.840 --> 00:07:22.130
with Michael's original story,

00:07:22.130 --> 00:07:24.940
so, no they don't technically
count as part of his history,

00:07:24.940 --> 00:07:26.440
but let's go over them briefly.

00:07:26.440 --> 00:07:28.750
Michael was sent to room with
a number of male patients,

00:07:28.750 --> 00:07:30.910
one of which was a psychopath
named Tony O'Malley

00:07:30.910 --> 00:07:33.010
who got into a scuffle with
Michael one night before bed

00:07:33.010 --> 00:07:34.840
and had to be separated
by a security guard.

00:07:34.840 --> 00:07:37.150
He was put off by Michaels
non-speaking nature

00:07:37.150 --> 00:07:38.870
and plans to attack him in his sleep,

00:07:38.870 --> 00:07:41.210
but Michael was not asleep
and shoved a crayon,

00:07:41.210 --> 00:07:43.290
or depending on where
you're from, a cray yawn,

00:07:43.290 --> 00:07:44.540
into Tony's left eye.

00:07:44.540 --> 00:07:47.140
Tony was actually one of the
few Michael victims to survive,

00:07:47.140 --> 00:07:50.190
but the crayon, or cray yawn,
pressed up against his brain,

00:07:50.190 --> 00:07:52.660
causing him to become more
delusional and violent,

00:07:52.660 --> 00:07:55.280
landing him in a padded cell
for solitary confinement.

00:07:55.280 --> 00:07:58.370
In November 1964, a
juvenile named Adrian Wade,

00:07:58.370 --> 00:08:00.130
who suffered from an
obsessive eating disorder,

00:08:00.130 --> 00:08:01.720
ate a cake that was intended for Michael,

00:08:01.720 --> 00:08:03.130
so Michael trapped him in the showers

00:08:03.130 --> 00:08:05.020
and tortured him with scalding hot water.

00:08:05.020 --> 00:08:07.120
He was found unconscious
with multiple burns,

00:08:07.120 --> 00:08:09.330
and later died in the hospital
wing of heart failure.

00:08:09.330 --> 00:08:11.040
Years would go by without incident,

00:08:11.040 --> 00:08:13.540
and most of the staff considered
Michael a model patient,

00:08:13.540 --> 00:08:16.150
but then in 1971, another young patient,

00:08:16.150 --> 00:08:18.380
a self-harmer named Roger,
who claimed to have witnessed

00:08:18.380 --> 00:08:19.860
Michael's attack on Tony O'Malley,

00:08:19.860 --> 00:08:22.120
was found after supposedly
biting off his own tongue

00:08:22.120 --> 00:08:23.070
and choking on it.

00:08:23.070 --> 00:08:23.908
If you're familiar with Michael,

00:08:23.908 --> 00:08:25.330
you can probably assume

00:08:25.330 --> 00:08:27.420
that that's not how
things really went down.

00:08:27.420 --> 00:08:29.237
That Halloween, one of the
asylum's administrators

00:08:29.237 --> 00:08:31.430
decided to put on a
Halloween party for the kids,

00:08:31.430 --> 00:08:32.890
and Michael wore a clown costume,

00:08:32.890 --> 00:08:35.970
the same costume he wore when
he jabbed Judith in 1963.

00:08:35.970 --> 00:08:38.360
A girl named Nancy teased
Michael for having cooties.

00:08:38.360 --> 00:08:40.000
During a game of bobbing for apples,

00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:42.247
lightning struck the building,
causing the power to go out,

00:08:42.247 --> 00:08:44.540
and in the cover of darkness,
Michael drowned her,

00:08:44.540 --> 00:08:46.142
and disappeared before
the lights came back up.

00:08:46.142 --> 00:08:48.780
When Loomis discovers what
happened, he is furious,

00:08:48.780 --> 00:08:50.960
frustrated by his patient's
continued silence,

00:08:50.960 --> 00:08:52.080
and nearly strikes the boy

00:08:52.080 --> 00:08:54.250
before being stopped by
his fiance, Jennifer.

00:08:54.250 --> 00:08:55.520
Jennifer mentions that she believes

00:08:55.520 --> 00:08:58.170
Michael belongs in a prison,
which Michael seems to hear,

00:08:58.170 --> 00:09:00.220
and he decides to make
her his next target.

00:09:00.220 --> 00:09:01.830
He throws her off the
roof of the building,

00:09:01.830 --> 00:09:04.450
and it is ruled that she
made the jump herself.

00:09:04.450 --> 00:09:07.110
What do all of these Chaos
Comics victims have in common?

00:09:07.110 --> 00:09:09.280
They all did something
Michael didn't like,

00:09:09.280 --> 00:09:11.736
whether it's aggression,
stolen food, accusations,

00:09:11.736 --> 00:09:14.020
general teasing or wishing ill on him,

00:09:14.020 --> 00:09:16.380
all of these characters
suffer from a form of revenge.

00:09:16.380 --> 00:09:18.920
In the Cult of Thorn arc,
that's not how Michael operates,

00:09:18.920 --> 00:09:20.450
he is driven by a supernatural evil

00:09:20.450 --> 00:09:22.350
that tells him what to
do and he has one goal,

00:09:22.350 --> 00:09:23.550
which we'll talk about later.

00:09:23.550 --> 00:09:25.750
That's part of why the comics
are not considered canon,

00:09:25.750 --> 00:09:27.220
so let's get back to what is canon,

00:09:27.220 --> 00:09:28.190
the original rampage

00:09:28.190 --> 00:09:32.237
that would take place on
Halloween night October 1978.

00:09:36.917 --> 00:09:39.334
(soft music)

00:09:41.070 --> 00:09:42.820
Michael Myers turns 21 years old,

00:09:42.820 --> 00:09:45.250
and so, was due back in court
to be tried as an adult.

00:09:45.250 --> 00:09:46.920
Dr. Loomis and Nurse Marion Chambers

00:09:46.920 --> 00:09:48.610
were supposed to transport
him to his trial,

00:09:48.610 --> 00:09:50.070
so Michael took action to make sure

00:09:50.070 --> 00:09:51.340
that this was not possible.

00:09:51.340 --> 00:09:52.830
He destroyed his room at Smith's Grove,

00:09:52.830 --> 00:09:54.240
freed many of his fellow captives,

00:09:54.240 --> 00:09:56.090
and left behind word "sister" in blood,

00:09:56.090 --> 00:09:57.740
although to most, this
appeared to be a reference

00:09:57.740 --> 00:09:59.010
to his older sister, Judith,

00:09:59.010 --> 00:10:00.510
because his younger sister's existence

00:10:00.510 --> 00:10:01.580
was hidden from the public,

00:10:01.580 --> 00:10:03.330
and she was given a
new name and new family

00:10:03.330 --> 00:10:04.300
so that she would be protected

00:10:04.300 --> 00:10:05.810
from any potential harassment.

00:10:05.810 --> 00:10:08.410
Since Dr. Wynn was the
administrator of the sanitarium,

00:10:08.410 --> 00:10:10.110
and also the leader of the Cult of Thorn,

00:10:10.110 --> 00:10:11.190
it's not hard to imagine

00:10:11.190 --> 00:10:12.930
that he didn't exactly try his hardest

00:10:12.930 --> 00:10:14.320
to prevent Michael's escape.

00:10:14.320 --> 00:10:15.870
Michael waits for Loomis and Chambers

00:10:15.870 --> 00:10:17.130
to pull up to the sanitarium,

00:10:17.130 --> 00:10:19.070
and when Loomis gets out
to use the nearby phone,

00:10:19.070 --> 00:10:21.260
he attacks Marion, driving
her out of the vehicle

00:10:21.260 --> 00:10:22.580
which he takes for himself.

00:10:22.580 --> 00:10:24.610
I know you can play as Michael
Myers in Dead by Daylight,

00:10:24.610 --> 00:10:25.550
but I think this is proof

00:10:25.550 --> 00:10:28.183
that he should also be playable in GTA.

00:10:28.183 --> 00:10:30.102
(phone rings)

00:10:30.102 --> 00:10:31.620
- [Roman] Let's go bowling.

00:10:31.620 --> 00:10:32.710
- [Zac] Michael's ability to drive

00:10:32.710 --> 00:10:34.300
without any training or experience

00:10:34.300 --> 00:10:35.870
has always been a point of question,

00:10:35.870 --> 00:10:37.610
one that's even brought up in the movie.

00:10:37.610 --> 00:10:39.740
- [Wynn] Sam, Haddonfield
is 150 miles away from here,

00:10:39.740 --> 00:10:41.330
now for God's sake, he can't drive a car!

00:10:41.330 --> 00:10:43.350
- He was doing very well last night.

00:10:43.350 --> 00:10:44.270
- When you consider the fact

00:10:44.270 --> 00:10:46.250
that Michael is no
ordinary mental patient,

00:10:46.250 --> 00:10:47.520
but rather more of a vessel

00:10:47.520 --> 00:10:49.210
for this ancient evil known as Thorn,

00:10:49.210 --> 00:10:50.810
this starts to make more sense.

00:10:50.810 --> 00:10:52.830
Throughout his story, we
discover many of the powers

00:10:52.830 --> 00:10:54.050
granted to him by Thorn,

00:10:54.050 --> 00:10:57.100
so the ability to operate a
car doesn't seem far fetched.

00:10:57.100 --> 00:11:00.040
During his 1978 rampage,
Michael is trying to recreate

00:11:00.040 --> 00:11:03.180
the experience he had when
killing his older sister in 1963.

00:11:03.180 --> 00:11:04.460
I like to think of it as a ritual

00:11:04.460 --> 00:11:05.830
that he established when he was six,

00:11:05.830 --> 00:11:07.040
going after his older sister,

00:11:07.040 --> 00:11:08.510
and now he's trying to recreate it

00:11:08.510 --> 00:11:10.010
going after his younger sister.

00:11:10.010 --> 00:11:12.197
When he was six, he wore a
one-piece clown suit and mask,

00:11:12.197 --> 00:11:13.520
his Halloween costume,

00:11:13.520 --> 00:11:15.700
so this time he puts
together a similar attire.

00:11:15.700 --> 00:11:18.070
He runs a mechanic's truck off
the road and annihilates him

00:11:18.070 --> 00:11:20.300
to get the one piece suit, and
when he gets into Haddonfield

00:11:20.300 --> 00:11:21.500
he breaks into the general store

00:11:21.500 --> 00:11:24.330
and steals his now iconic mask,
in place of the clown mask.

00:11:24.330 --> 00:11:26.480
He also steals some rope,
which he would use later.

00:11:26.480 --> 00:11:29.080
Next, he breaks into his old
home, which now sits abandoned.

00:11:29.080 --> 00:11:31.550
When they later investigate the
house, they find a dead dog,

00:11:31.550 --> 00:11:33.456
which Loomis has his own explanation for.

00:11:33.456 --> 00:11:35.060
- He got hungry.

00:11:35.060 --> 00:11:36.630
- Okay, he knows his patient best,

00:11:36.630 --> 00:11:38.700
so I'm willing to accept that explanation.

00:11:38.700 --> 00:11:40.930
At this point his sister,
Laurie, stops by the house

00:11:40.930 --> 00:11:42.110
to leave a key under the mat

00:11:42.110 --> 00:11:43.620
at the request of her adoptive father,

00:11:43.620 --> 00:11:45.800
who is a realtor who's
trying to sell the place.

00:11:45.800 --> 00:11:47.460
Michael sees her walk up to the front door

00:11:47.460 --> 00:11:49.330
and leave the key, but
he lets her walk away,

00:11:49.330 --> 00:11:51.740
and stares at her as she makes
her way towards her school.

00:11:51.740 --> 00:11:54.530
Did Michael immediately know
that this was his sister,

00:11:54.530 --> 00:11:55.760
or did Laurie become a target

00:11:55.760 --> 00:11:57.040
simply because he was angry

00:11:57.040 --> 00:11:58.670
that his old house was being sold?

00:11:58.670 --> 00:12:00.170
We'll get our answer a little bit later,

00:12:00.170 --> 00:12:01.440
but for now, we just need to know

00:12:01.440 --> 00:12:02.850
that Michael was planning to make Laurie

00:12:02.850 --> 00:12:04.270
one of his future victims.

00:12:04.270 --> 00:12:06.520
I also wondered why he stalks
Laurie throughout the day

00:12:06.520 --> 00:12:08.120
instead of just killing her right now.

00:12:08.120 --> 00:12:08.980
He follows her to school

00:12:08.980 --> 00:12:10.160
and stares her down through the window

00:12:10.160 --> 00:12:11.200
during her English class,

00:12:11.200 --> 00:12:12.354
then after killing some time skulking

00:12:12.354 --> 00:12:13.750
around the elementary school,

00:12:13.750 --> 00:12:15.300
keeps surveillance on
Laurie and her friends

00:12:15.300 --> 00:12:16.570
as they walk home from school.

00:12:16.570 --> 00:12:18.570
When Annie yells out at him, he even stops

00:12:18.570 --> 00:12:20.910
and seems to consider killing
them all right then and there,

00:12:20.910 --> 00:12:21.743
but doesn't.

00:12:21.743 --> 00:12:23.040
So what's the big hold up?

00:12:23.040 --> 00:12:23.873
Obviously the real reason

00:12:23.873 --> 00:12:25.750
is that the movie would
only be 22 minutes long

00:12:25.750 --> 00:12:26.810
if he killed them in daylight,

00:12:26.810 --> 00:12:29.590
but also in 1963, Michael given his curse

00:12:29.590 --> 00:12:31.280
as part of the Festival of Samhain.

00:12:31.280 --> 00:12:32.113
- [Loomis] Sam Hain.

00:12:32.113 --> 00:12:33.990
- And if we go back to
the holiday's origins

00:12:33.990 --> 00:12:34.870
in Celtic Ireland,

00:12:34.870 --> 00:12:38.100
it was celebrated starting in
the evening on October 31st.

00:12:38.100 --> 00:12:39.650
- [Annie] Subtle, isn't he?

00:12:39.650 --> 00:12:41.390
- So if Michael is waiting for nightfall

00:12:41.390 --> 00:12:42.440
for the sake of tradition,

00:12:42.440 --> 00:12:44.590
that may also explain what he does next.

00:12:44.590 --> 00:12:47.180
He stops by the cemetery and
steals his sister's tombstone,

00:12:47.180 --> 00:12:48.520
with plans to use it as a prop

00:12:48.520 --> 00:12:50.270
during his recreation of her death.

00:12:50.270 --> 00:12:52.330
Instead of an immediate
sibling slice and dice,

00:12:52.330 --> 00:12:53.550
he just keeps an eye on Laurie,

00:12:53.550 --> 00:12:54.940
staring from behind some hedges,

00:12:54.940 --> 00:12:56.320
watching her through her bedroom window,

00:12:56.320 --> 00:12:57.380
and following her and Annie

00:12:57.380 --> 00:12:59.360
as they head to their
babysitting jobs that evening.

00:12:59.360 --> 00:13:00.950
When they arrive, he
waits for them to park

00:13:00.950 --> 00:13:02.617
and watches them go to
their respective jobs.

00:13:02.617 --> 00:13:04.960
Remember, if you've seen my
Things You Missed episode

00:13:04.960 --> 00:13:06.000
on the original Halloween,

00:13:06.000 --> 00:13:07.840
you saw me provide a
different interpretation

00:13:07.840 --> 00:13:09.340
for Michael's behavior that afternoon,

00:13:09.340 --> 00:13:12.030
because I was analyzing the
movie as a stand alone story.

00:13:12.030 --> 00:13:13.330
But in this Horror History episode,

00:13:13.330 --> 00:13:15.140
I'm analyzing Michael's entire character,

00:13:15.140 --> 00:13:17.320
and the context provided by
the sequels in this timeline

00:13:17.320 --> 00:13:18.650
changes how I have to look at him.

00:13:18.650 --> 00:13:20.160
It's all about the family connection

00:13:20.160 --> 00:13:22.320
because Michael has to
sacrifice his entire family

00:13:22.320 --> 00:13:23.860
before being freed by Thorn.

00:13:23.860 --> 00:13:25.190
Of course, having a massive amount

00:13:25.190 --> 00:13:26.550
of retroactive continuity like this

00:13:26.550 --> 00:13:28.680
can kind of mess up the
story if you aren't careful,

00:13:28.680 --> 00:13:30.610
and let's face it, this isn't Saw,

00:13:30.610 --> 00:13:32.440
the continuity wasn't the biggest concern.

00:13:32.440 --> 00:13:33.750
So the next thing that Michael does

00:13:33.750 --> 00:13:35.160
is go after the sex-crazed teens

00:13:35.160 --> 00:13:36.900
babysitting across the
street from the Doyle house

00:13:36.900 --> 00:13:38.090
where Laurie is babysitting.

00:13:38.090 --> 00:13:40.490
If I'm gonna try to slap on a
reasoning for his actions here

00:13:40.490 --> 00:13:42.650
the curse of Thorn is what's
telling Michael what to do,

00:13:42.650 --> 00:13:44.410
and Thorn likes human sacrifice,

00:13:44.410 --> 00:13:46.870
so any extra victims that
Michael can decease along the way

00:13:46.870 --> 00:13:47.703
are bonus points,

00:13:47.703 --> 00:13:49.440
even if they aren't a
part of Michael's family.

00:13:49.440 --> 00:13:51.480
It's like how I might go
out to get a steak taco,

00:13:51.480 --> 00:13:53.680
but once I see the menu I'm
probably gonna add the nachos,

00:13:53.680 --> 00:13:55.340
cinnamon twists, horchata,

00:13:55.340 --> 00:13:57.400
and probably like three
additional steak tacos

00:13:57.400 --> 00:13:58.340
if we're being real.

00:13:58.340 --> 00:13:59.690
The way Michael goes after his victims

00:13:59.690 --> 00:14:02.320
can only be described
with one word, unsettling.

00:14:02.320 --> 00:14:04.070
Everything he does is very methodical,

00:14:04.070 --> 00:14:06.610
from his slow walking, to
his empty staring into space,

00:14:06.610 --> 00:14:08.440
to his complete silence as he does it all.

00:14:08.440 --> 00:14:09.430
This creates the impression

00:14:09.430 --> 00:14:11.910
that he's essentially a blank
slate, void of character,

00:14:11.910 --> 00:14:13.830
almost like a machine
programmed by the curse

00:14:13.830 --> 00:14:14.950
that has been placed on him.

00:14:14.950 --> 00:14:16.810
This not only fits the
idea of the character,

00:14:16.810 --> 00:14:18.680
essentially being a shape
that does these things

00:14:18.680 --> 00:14:20.250
without interjecting any personality,

00:14:20.250 --> 00:14:22.350
but also taps into elements
that the human mind

00:14:22.350 --> 00:14:23.640
perceives as unsettling.

00:14:23.640 --> 00:14:25.920
The core reason that people
can be easily off-put

00:14:25.920 --> 00:14:27.130
by the idea of voyeurism

00:14:27.130 --> 00:14:29.160
goes back to basic survival instinct.

00:14:29.160 --> 00:14:29.993
When humans lived in the wild,

00:14:29.993 --> 00:14:32.290
if another lurking
animal had eyes on them,

00:14:32.290 --> 00:14:34.740
it was most likely a predator
getting ready to strike.

00:14:34.740 --> 00:14:36.320
So we're genetically predisposed

00:14:36.320 --> 00:14:38.970
to be uncomfortable in these
situations and avoid them.

00:14:38.970 --> 00:14:41.120
One of the first studies on
the sensation of being watched

00:14:41.120 --> 00:14:42.940
was called "The Feeling
of Being Stared At,"

00:14:42.940 --> 00:14:44.453
a title almost as fitting to it's content

00:14:44.453 --> 00:14:46.960
as the title of that
80s movie with the blob

00:14:46.960 --> 00:14:48.440
which was called, "The Blob."

00:14:48.440 --> 00:14:50.420
The article's author, Dr. Edward Titchener

00:14:50.420 --> 00:14:52.490
disproves the idea that
someone's gaze itself

00:14:52.490 --> 00:14:54.030
could be what gives you those goosebumps.

00:14:54.030 --> 00:14:55.360
That unsettled feeling you get

00:14:55.360 --> 00:14:56.950
is something you give yourself.

00:14:56.950 --> 00:14:59.470
In fact, an actual voyeur
isn't even necessary,

00:14:59.470 --> 00:15:00.954
you can get creeped out just by believing

00:15:00.954 --> 00:15:02.400
that you are being watched.

00:15:02.400 --> 00:15:04.420
Michael takes advantage
of this by popping in,

00:15:04.420 --> 00:15:05.767
being seen by the victim
that he's stalking,

00:15:05.767 --> 00:15:08.340
and then disappearing,
leaving his target to wonder

00:15:08.340 --> 00:15:09.740
if he's still somewhere nearby,

00:15:09.740 --> 00:15:12.066
zeroing in on them with
that piercing stare.

00:15:12.066 --> 00:15:15.309
- Laurie, the Boogeyman's outside, look.

00:15:16.767 --> 00:15:18.070
- Tommy, there's nobody outside.

00:15:18.070 --> 00:15:19.070
- But it would not be long

00:15:19.070 --> 00:15:20.940
before Michael Myers's apparent voyeurism

00:15:20.940 --> 00:15:23.773
would escalate into much
more dangerous behavior.

00:15:32.700 --> 00:15:33.820
Michael's night continues

00:15:33.820 --> 00:15:35.380
as he focuses on Laurie's friend Annie,

00:15:35.380 --> 00:15:37.550
who is babysitting at the
Wallace house across the street.

00:15:37.550 --> 00:15:39.210
He starts by locking
her in the laundry room,

00:15:39.210 --> 00:15:40.310
then after she gets out,

00:15:40.310 --> 00:15:42.800
he eavesdrops as she makes
evening plans with her boyfriend.

00:15:42.800 --> 00:15:44.450
And by evening plans, I mean se...

00:15:44.450 --> 00:15:45.530
Michael hides inside of her car

00:15:45.530 --> 00:15:46.840
as she drops off the little girl, Lindsey,

00:15:46.840 --> 00:15:48.010
across the street at the Doyle's house,

00:15:48.010 --> 00:15:49.770
and when she comes back
she hops into the vehicle

00:15:49.770 --> 00:15:50.640
to go pick up Paul,

00:15:50.640 --> 00:15:52.490
and he lets her discover
that she's not alone

00:15:52.490 --> 00:15:54.160
before getting down to business.

00:15:54.160 --> 00:15:56.375
And by business, I mean killing her.

00:15:56.375 --> 00:15:59.125
(dramatic music)

00:16:00.770 --> 00:16:02.450
He didn't even have the
courtesy to phone Paul

00:16:02.450 --> 00:16:04.090
and let him know that
his ride is cancelled.

00:16:04.090 --> 00:16:06.310
He moves Annie's body
inside for later use.

00:16:06.310 --> 00:16:07.420
When he comes back downstairs,

00:16:07.420 --> 00:16:09.520
he discovers two more
horny teens have appeared,

00:16:09.520 --> 00:16:10.910
Linda and her boyfriend Bob,

00:16:10.910 --> 00:16:12.290
who were getting at it on the couch.

00:16:12.290 --> 00:16:13.520
After they move things upstairs,

00:16:13.520 --> 00:16:15.230
Bob heads down to the kitchen for a drink,

00:16:15.230 --> 00:16:17.240
and Michael surprises him by doing this.

00:16:18.273 --> 00:16:21.820
(dramatic music)

00:16:21.820 --> 00:16:23.580
He pins Bob to the wall
with a butcher's knife,

00:16:23.580 --> 00:16:25.140
then further conceals his identity

00:16:25.140 --> 00:16:26.860
by dressing up as a bedsheet ghost

00:16:26.860 --> 00:16:28.840
which, I mean, if he
wanted to pretend to be Bob

00:16:28.840 --> 00:16:31.360
in order to trick Linda,
he's already in a costume,

00:16:31.360 --> 00:16:32.810
he's rocking the mask and jumpsuit.

00:16:32.810 --> 00:16:34.980
But I guess the bedsheet
ghost maybe does a better job

00:16:34.980 --> 00:16:36.200
of concealing his physique,

00:16:36.200 --> 00:16:38.500
because he's much more
physically imposing than Bob.

00:16:38.500 --> 00:16:40.340
Putting Bob's glasses
over the ghost costume

00:16:40.340 --> 00:16:42.500
is enough to convince Linda
that that's her boyfriend,

00:16:42.500 --> 00:16:44.330
and when she turns her
back to him to call Laurie,

00:16:44.330 --> 00:16:45.860
he strangles her with the phone cord.

00:16:45.860 --> 00:16:47.700
With all three of Laurie's
friends across the street

00:16:47.700 --> 00:16:48.533
out of commission,

00:16:48.533 --> 00:16:50.570
Michael turns out the last
remaining lights in the house,

00:16:50.570 --> 00:16:52.160
much like how the sanitarium went dark

00:16:52.160 --> 00:16:54.940
before he took out his
fellow patient Nancy in 1971.

00:16:54.940 --> 00:16:56.410
He then arranges the body of Annie

00:16:56.410 --> 00:16:58.680
in the upstairs bedroom under
the Judith Myers's tombstone

00:16:58.680 --> 00:17:00.360
as a tribute to his first ever attack,

00:17:00.360 --> 00:17:02.670
and waits for his younger
sister to stumble upon it.

00:17:02.670 --> 00:17:03.840
Linda is stuffed in a closet

00:17:03.840 --> 00:17:05.100
and Bob is hung up in the closet

00:17:05.100 --> 00:17:06.450
with the rope he stole earlier.

00:17:06.450 --> 00:17:07.283
Good planning.

00:17:07.283 --> 00:17:09.310
After discovering this, Laurie
stumbles out of the room

00:17:09.310 --> 00:17:10.350
in a mess of emotions,

00:17:10.350 --> 00:17:12.990
and Michael emerges from the
darkness of the room next door,

00:17:12.990 --> 00:17:15.220
in what is probably the
coolest shot in Halloween.

00:17:15.220 --> 00:17:16.590
She is chased back across the street,

00:17:16.590 --> 00:17:17.680
and tries to defend herself

00:17:17.680 --> 00:17:19.300
by sticking a knitting
needle through his neck,

00:17:19.300 --> 00:17:21.570
which does cause him to drop
to the floor for some time.

00:17:21.570 --> 00:17:22.570
If you're watching this video,

00:17:22.570 --> 00:17:25.440
you probably already know that
Michael Myers is invincible,

00:17:25.440 --> 00:17:27.260
and this is a result of
the powers he acquires

00:17:27.260 --> 00:17:29.400
by being cursed by the
ancient demon, Thorn.

00:17:29.400 --> 00:17:31.901
But at the same time, he isn't
just an unstoppable machine.

00:17:31.901 --> 00:17:33.560
Hurting him enough will put him down

00:17:33.560 --> 00:17:34.560
for short periods of time,

00:17:34.560 --> 00:17:36.820
which I refer to as his "recharge period."

00:17:36.820 --> 00:17:39.190
When he comes back to, he
follows Laurie up the stairs

00:17:39.190 --> 00:17:40.560
and finds her tending to the kids,

00:17:40.560 --> 00:17:42.430
but now his focus is on his sister.

00:17:42.430 --> 00:17:44.820
He finds her hiding in a bedroom
closet and busts through.

00:17:44.820 --> 00:17:46.660
Lights on? No! Lights off.

00:17:46.660 --> 00:17:48.900
Laurie resourcefully pokes his
eye out with a coat hanger,

00:17:48.900 --> 00:17:50.020
which puts him down long enough

00:17:50.020 --> 00:17:50.990
for her to get out of the room

00:17:50.990 --> 00:17:52.440
and get the kids out of the house.

00:17:52.440 --> 00:17:53.940
Michael gets a quick ab workout in,

00:17:53.940 --> 00:17:55.270
and then comes for her once more

00:17:55.270 --> 00:17:57.340
and she's only just able
to rip off his mask,

00:17:57.340 --> 00:17:59.140
which completely shocks him for a moment.

00:17:59.140 --> 00:18:01.710
This is one of the few times
we see his face as an adult,

00:18:01.710 --> 00:18:03.630
and he looks shocked, almost like the mask

00:18:03.630 --> 00:18:05.270
is such an important part of this ritual

00:18:05.270 --> 00:18:06.960
that he can't believe she's removed it.

00:18:06.960 --> 00:18:09.500
As he puts it back on, he's
shot by someone in the dark

00:18:09.500 --> 00:18:10.601
and stumbles back into the bedroom.

00:18:10.601 --> 00:18:13.610
It turns out to be his old
psychiatrist Dr. Loomis,

00:18:13.610 --> 00:18:15.020
who unloads five more bullets into him,

00:18:15.020 --> 00:18:17.650
knocking him off the patio and
onto the Doyle's front lawn.

00:18:17.650 --> 00:18:20.190
But as always, Michael's
ailment is only temporary,

00:18:20.190 --> 00:18:21.820
and he flees the scene to recoup.

00:18:21.820 --> 00:18:23.070
He hides out in a back alley

00:18:23.070 --> 00:18:24.960
as the police close in on the Doyle house.

00:18:24.960 --> 00:18:26.010
Now left without a weapon,

00:18:26.010 --> 00:18:28.000
he goes up to a random
residence to restock,

00:18:28.000 --> 00:18:29.360
and arms himself with a carving knife

00:18:29.360 --> 00:18:31.090
stolen from Mrs. Elrod's cutting board.

00:18:31.090 --> 00:18:32.328
Then, just to make sure the knife works,

00:18:32.328 --> 00:18:35.240
I guess, he breaks into the
house of their neighbor, Alice

00:18:35.240 --> 00:18:37.290
and successfully tests it out on her.

00:18:37.290 --> 00:18:39.670
I could try to dissect
why the Elrods got to live

00:18:39.670 --> 00:18:42.330
and Alice didn't but I
think it's better not to.

00:18:42.330 --> 00:18:44.410
Part of what makes this
iteration of Michael scary

00:18:44.410 --> 00:18:46.330
for audiences is his unpredictability,

00:18:46.330 --> 00:18:48.300
you don't really know
when he's going to strike.

00:18:48.300 --> 00:18:49.490
This must be when Michael broke

00:18:49.490 --> 00:18:51.570
into his old Elementary
School and left this clue

00:18:51.570 --> 00:18:53.150
that would later be found by police.

00:18:53.150 --> 00:18:55.240
It's a child-like drawing
of a family on Halloween,

00:18:55.240 --> 00:18:56.550
potentially Michael's family,

00:18:56.550 --> 00:18:58.070
with a knife stuck into the sister.

00:18:58.070 --> 00:19:00.380
On the left, there seems to
already be a discarded body,

00:19:00.380 --> 00:19:01.950
which probably represents Judith,

00:19:01.950 --> 00:19:03.500
meaning that this girl
with the knife in her

00:19:03.500 --> 00:19:05.090
most likely represents Laurie,

00:19:05.090 --> 00:19:07.080
and this answers one of
our questions from earlier

00:19:07.080 --> 00:19:08.060
on in this video.

00:19:08.060 --> 00:19:09.920
Initially, it was unclear if Michael knew

00:19:09.920 --> 00:19:12.130
that Laurie was his other
sister when he first spotted her

00:19:12.130 --> 00:19:12.963
at the Myers house,

00:19:12.963 --> 00:19:14.810
and I speculated that
maybe he went after her

00:19:14.810 --> 00:19:16.880
because he was simply
upset that she was involved

00:19:16.880 --> 00:19:19.160
in his childhood home being
put on the real estate market.

00:19:19.160 --> 00:19:21.880
So this drawing, if I'm
interpreting it correctly,

00:19:21.880 --> 00:19:23.470
which will surely be up for debate,

00:19:23.470 --> 00:19:25.120
would prove that he did know about Laurie

00:19:25.120 --> 00:19:26.870
and he was targeting her specifically.

00:19:26.870 --> 00:19:28.380
He also paints the word Samhain...

00:19:28.380 --> 00:19:29.300
- [Loomis] Sam Hain.

00:19:29.300 --> 00:19:30.133
- [Zac] Onto the chalkboard

00:19:30.133 --> 00:19:31.960
as a tribute to his demonic lord Thorn,

00:19:31.960 --> 00:19:33.580
since the Curse of Thorn
that has afflicted him

00:19:33.580 --> 00:19:35.245
all these years is part
of a ritual carried out

00:19:35.245 --> 00:19:37.080
during the Festival of Samhain.

00:19:37.080 --> 00:19:38.000
- [Loomis] Sam Hain.

00:19:38.000 --> 00:19:39.650
- It seems like the
lesson on the chalkboard

00:19:39.650 --> 00:19:41.530
may have already been
there when Michael arrived,

00:19:41.530 --> 00:19:43.407
but it's also possible
that it's no coincidence,

00:19:43.407 --> 00:19:45.430
seeing as how it's an astronomy lesson,

00:19:45.430 --> 00:19:47.350
and the date of each of
Michael's homicidal rampages

00:19:47.350 --> 00:19:49.550
is determined by the alignment of planets

00:19:49.550 --> 00:19:50.430
in the solar system.

00:19:50.430 --> 00:19:52.380
At this point, news of
a killer in Haddonfield

00:19:52.380 --> 00:19:53.640
is spreading all over the media,

00:19:53.640 --> 00:19:55.195
which at the time meant TV and radios,

00:19:55.195 --> 00:19:57.490
and Michael overhears where
Laurie is being taken,

00:19:57.490 --> 00:19:58.850
from this cowboy's boombox.

00:19:58.850 --> 00:20:00.083
Yee-haw, roll it.

00:20:02.380 --> 00:20:04.010
- [On Radio] There is one survivor,

00:20:04.010 --> 00:20:05.640
17-year old Laurie Strode

00:20:05.640 --> 00:20:07.840
was found directly across
the street from the home

00:20:07.840 --> 00:20:09.590
where the murders took place.

00:20:09.590 --> 00:20:11.290
The teenager was taken across town

00:20:11.290 --> 00:20:13.111
to Haddonfield Memorial Clinic.

00:20:13.111 --> 00:20:15.030
(eerie music)

00:20:15.030 --> 00:20:15.863
- It must have been getting close

00:20:15.863 --> 00:20:17.140
to Michael's bedtime or something,

00:20:17.140 --> 00:20:18.130
because after hearing this,

00:20:18.130 --> 00:20:20.750
he just lets the next 17
teenagers he crosses paths with

00:20:20.750 --> 00:20:21.583
go free.

00:20:21.583 --> 00:20:23.690
Seriously, I counted, he just
goes straight to the hospital

00:20:23.690 --> 00:20:25.170
and dumps out the rest
of his cherry slurpee

00:20:25.170 --> 00:20:26.003
in the dumpster.

00:20:26.003 --> 00:20:28.020
He promptly heads downstairs
to hide in the nursery,

00:20:28.020 --> 00:20:29.640
before continuing on to the store room

00:20:29.640 --> 00:20:31.500
where he's able to slash
through the phone lines,

00:20:31.500 --> 00:20:33.660
effectively isolating Laurie
and the hospital staff

00:20:33.660 --> 00:20:34.940
from calling in outside help.

00:20:34.940 --> 00:20:36.970
One by one, he takes out
each of the staff members

00:20:36.970 --> 00:20:38.520
at the hospital taking care of Laurie,

00:20:38.520 --> 00:20:40.370
starting with the security
guard Mr. Garrett,

00:20:40.370 --> 00:20:42.200
who gets tomahawked with
the pointy end of a hammer,

00:20:42.200 --> 00:20:44.640
and then an EMT named Bud
gets choked from behind

00:20:44.640 --> 00:20:46.260
after making love to his girlfriend Karen

00:20:46.260 --> 00:20:47.520
in a hydrotherapy bath.

00:20:47.520 --> 00:20:49.460
After doing so, he cranks
up the heat of the bath

00:20:49.460 --> 00:20:53.373
to over 130°F in preparation
of his next kill.

00:21:02.420 --> 00:21:04.360
Remember how Michael used a ghost costume,

00:21:04.360 --> 00:21:06.440
pretending to be Bob in
order to get close to Linda

00:21:06.440 --> 00:21:07.450
earlier that evening?

00:21:07.450 --> 00:21:09.030
Now, Michael pretends to be Bud

00:21:09.030 --> 00:21:11.200
while Karen's back is turned,
and when he gets close enough,

00:21:11.200 --> 00:21:12.820
he dunks her repeatedly in the bath.

00:21:12.820 --> 00:21:15.614
In my opinion this takes the
cake in terms of brutality.

00:21:15.614 --> 00:21:16.530
- Brutality!

00:21:16.530 --> 00:21:18.140
- They say that burning and drowning

00:21:18.140 --> 00:21:20.180
are the two most painful ways to die,

00:21:20.180 --> 00:21:22.120
and this is a combination of both.

00:21:22.120 --> 00:21:23.630
In fact, if you look at TheTopTens,

00:21:23.630 --> 00:21:25.100
which is a website that lets the internet

00:21:25.100 --> 00:21:26.110
vote on ranking things,

00:21:26.110 --> 00:21:28.110
people have agreed that
burning to death and drowning

00:21:28.110 --> 00:21:29.740
would be the worst two ways to go.

00:21:29.740 --> 00:21:31.240
Of course, we'll never know for sure,

00:21:31.240 --> 00:21:33.500
seeing as how everyone who
participated in this poll

00:21:33.500 --> 00:21:35.750
was still alive but you get the idea.

00:21:35.750 --> 00:21:38.150
On top of that, I can only
imagine the stark terror

00:21:38.150 --> 00:21:39.040
that Karen felt,

00:21:39.040 --> 00:21:41.100
because she thought she was
in the safe protective hands

00:21:41.100 --> 00:21:42.859
of her boyfriend, and she
turns around to realize

00:21:42.859 --> 00:21:45.510
that it's actually this
terrifying masked man.

00:21:45.510 --> 00:21:46.570
She's also undressed,

00:21:46.570 --> 00:21:48.610
so add a feeling of
vulnerability to the equation,

00:21:48.610 --> 00:21:50.320
and this is just not an ideal way

00:21:50.320 --> 00:21:51.800
to spend your final moments.

00:21:51.800 --> 00:21:53.473
It seems like Michael just
wants to clear out anyone

00:21:53.473 --> 00:21:56.120
who could pose as an obstacle
to him getting to Laurie,

00:21:56.120 --> 00:21:57.310
and the next person in his way

00:21:57.310 --> 00:21:59.490
was most likely Nurse Virginia Alves.

00:21:59.490 --> 00:22:01.290
Michael catches her in
one of the surgery rooms

00:22:01.290 --> 00:22:02.980
and ties her down to an operating table,

00:22:02.980 --> 00:22:04.950
then hooks her up to
a severed IV catheter,

00:22:04.950 --> 00:22:06.010
so she's unable to move

00:22:06.010 --> 00:22:08.140
as her blood slowly
drains out of her body.

00:22:08.140 --> 00:22:10.450
He continues to the office
of Dr. Frederick Mixter

00:22:10.450 --> 00:22:12.620
and prescribes him with
20 CCs of medication,

00:22:12.620 --> 00:22:14.470
injected directly into his right eye,

00:22:14.470 --> 00:22:16.750
then when Nurse Janet Marshall
comes to check on him,

00:22:16.750 --> 00:22:18.060
Michael appears out of the dark

00:22:18.060 --> 00:22:19.600
and jabs the blood vessel in her temple

00:22:19.600 --> 00:22:20.760
with an air-filled syringe,

00:22:20.760 --> 00:22:22.920
which essentially creates an
air bubble in your bloodstream

00:22:22.920 --> 00:22:24.460
and stops the flow of blood to the brain,

00:22:24.460 --> 00:22:25.600
which is usually lethal.

00:22:25.600 --> 00:22:27.010
It seems his very straightforward

00:22:27.010 --> 00:22:28.610
and methodical way of going about things,

00:22:28.610 --> 00:22:30.280
doesn't hold him back
from getting creative

00:22:30.280 --> 00:22:31.460
with some of his kills.

00:22:31.460 --> 00:22:33.580
With all of the staff that
regularly walk the corridors

00:22:33.580 --> 00:22:36.010
of the main lobby either
dead or trying to find help,

00:22:36.010 --> 00:22:37.990
Michael has free reign
to slow-walk his way

00:22:37.990 --> 00:22:39.860
right into Laurie's room uncontested.

00:22:39.860 --> 00:22:41.410
Now armed with a surgical scalpel,

00:22:41.410 --> 00:22:43.240
he sees his target apparently unconscious

00:22:43.240 --> 00:22:46.126
due to the medication she's
on, and decides to get stabby.

00:22:46.126 --> 00:22:48.626
(eerie music)

00:22:52.350 --> 00:22:53.810
When he realizes she's not there,

00:22:53.810 --> 00:22:55.770
he looks to the security
monitors to find her,

00:22:55.770 --> 00:22:56.840
and heads in her direction,

00:22:56.840 --> 00:22:58.500
but first he comes across a conversation

00:22:58.500 --> 00:23:00.600
between the last two
remaining hospital employees,

00:23:00.600 --> 00:23:01.780
a nurse named Jill Franco

00:23:01.780 --> 00:23:03.630
and an ambulance attendant named Jimmy.

00:23:03.630 --> 00:23:04.760
He overhears Jimmy instruct her

00:23:04.760 --> 00:23:05.830
to drive to the Sheriff's Station for help

00:23:05.830 --> 00:23:07.960
if she doesn't find
anyone in the east wing,

00:23:07.960 --> 00:23:09.700
so while she's searching the
other side of the building,

00:23:09.700 --> 00:23:11.070
Michael goes out to the parking lot

00:23:11.070 --> 00:23:12.440
and disables all of the vehicles,

00:23:12.440 --> 00:23:14.840
by stabbing the tires and
cutting their fuel lines.

00:23:14.840 --> 00:23:16.020
As Jill comes back in,

00:23:16.020 --> 00:23:17.730
Michael hears her
calling out Laurie's name

00:23:17.730 --> 00:23:18.980
and goes towards the sound.

00:23:18.980 --> 00:23:20.550
Just before she realizes he's there,

00:23:20.550 --> 00:23:22.690
he drives the scalpel
into her back so hard

00:23:22.690 --> 00:23:24.340
that he's able to lift
her up off the ground,

00:23:24.340 --> 00:23:26.680
with the small blade holding
up her entire weight.

00:23:26.680 --> 00:23:28.410
This is where another one of the abilities

00:23:28.410 --> 00:23:30.590
that The Curse has granted
him starts to become clear,

00:23:30.590 --> 00:23:31.730
in addition to being immortal,

00:23:31.730 --> 00:23:33.960
he's also acquired superhuman strength.

00:23:33.960 --> 00:23:35.630
With one more staff member out of the way

00:23:35.630 --> 00:23:37.770
and his main target finally
in his line of sight again,

00:23:37.770 --> 00:23:38.630
he goes after her,

00:23:38.630 --> 00:23:40.880
but his refusal to walk
anywhere near a normal pace

00:23:40.880 --> 00:23:42.020
doesn't do him any favors,

00:23:42.020 --> 00:23:43.360
and Laurie gets away in an elevator.

00:23:43.360 --> 00:23:46.110
However it's not long before
Michael catches her outside,

00:23:46.110 --> 00:23:47.070
how 'bout that?

00:23:47.070 --> 00:23:48.310
He's almost able to reach her,

00:23:48.310 --> 00:23:50.240
before someone lets her
back into the building.

00:23:50.240 --> 00:23:51.660
Michael just crashes through the door

00:23:51.660 --> 00:23:53.666
like a deer in a hair salon.

00:23:53.666 --> 00:23:54.580
(screams)

00:23:54.580 --> 00:23:56.340
And sees Dr. Loomis and Nurse Chambers

00:23:56.340 --> 00:23:57.480
trying to protect Laurie.

00:23:57.480 --> 00:23:59.240
His old psychiatrist is armed and ready,

00:23:59.240 --> 00:24:00.610
and shoots him five more times,

00:24:00.610 --> 00:24:02.850
bringing the grand total
to 11 on the night.

00:24:02.850 --> 00:24:05.150
As we've seen to be the case
whenever Michael is attacked,

00:24:05.150 --> 00:24:07.420
he collapses temporarily, but cannot die.

00:24:07.420 --> 00:24:09.040
The state marshal that
came with Dr. Loomis

00:24:09.040 --> 00:24:10.160
goes in for a closer look,

00:24:10.160 --> 00:24:12.350
stupidly assuming that
Michael had stopped breathing,

00:24:12.350 --> 00:24:14.510
and Michael springs to
life and slits his throat.

00:24:14.510 --> 00:24:16.640
Loomis and Laurie retreat
to another operating room,

00:24:16.640 --> 00:24:18.300
so Michael busts down that door too,

00:24:18.300 --> 00:24:20.360
bringing him within striking
distance of his doctor.

00:24:20.360 --> 00:24:21.350
Loomis's gun jams,

00:24:21.350 --> 00:24:23.630
and Michael takes the opportunity
to stab him in the gut.

00:24:23.630 --> 00:24:25.900
When he corners Laurie, she
fires a couple shots at him,

00:24:25.900 --> 00:24:28.230
which apparently land just
above his eyes I guess?

00:24:28.230 --> 00:24:29.063
Judging by the fact

00:24:29.063 --> 00:24:30.660
that the mask doesn't
have any bullet holes?

00:24:30.660 --> 00:24:32.790
The drip down from his wounds
temporarily blinds him,

00:24:32.790 --> 00:24:35.190
and rather than just using his
hearing to try to locate her,

00:24:35.190 --> 00:24:36.810
he just kind of flails around the room

00:24:36.810 --> 00:24:37.760
in the general direction

00:24:37.760 --> 00:24:39.550
where he thinks she
might be for some reason.

00:24:39.550 --> 00:24:41.290
Laurie is audibly whimpering too,

00:24:41.290 --> 00:24:42.900
so it should have been kind of easy.

00:24:42.900 --> 00:24:44.630
Not one of Michael's finer moments.

00:24:44.630 --> 00:24:46.930
Somehow though, he is able
to hear the hissing sound

00:24:46.930 --> 00:24:48.280
of gas tanks being opened by Loomis

00:24:48.280 --> 00:24:49.150
near the front of the room,

00:24:49.150 --> 00:24:51.230
but before long the sound surrounds him.

00:24:51.230 --> 00:24:54.230
The last thing he hears is
the voice of his psychiatrist.

00:24:54.230 --> 00:24:55.900
- It is time, Michael.

00:24:56.964 --> 00:24:59.820
- What the fu-- (BOOM)

00:24:59.820 --> 00:25:01.022
- This is easily the biggest blast

00:25:01.022 --> 00:25:03.020
that Mr. Myers has yet to endure.

00:25:03.020 --> 00:25:04.346
With the mechanics of his invincibility

00:25:04.346 --> 00:25:06.700
and recharge period
still mostly a mystery,

00:25:06.700 --> 00:25:08.870
I can only assume that it
was his sheer willpower

00:25:08.870 --> 00:25:10.590
and determination that kept him going,

00:25:10.590 --> 00:25:13.210
because he knew he was so close
to finishing his sister off.

00:25:13.210 --> 00:25:15.260
He was able to force himself
to go a little bit longer

00:25:15.260 --> 00:25:16.260
before collapsing again,

00:25:16.260 --> 00:25:18.740
as he had when suffering
would-be fatal blows in the past.

00:25:18.740 --> 00:25:20.540
So to Laurie's absolute horror,

00:25:20.540 --> 00:25:22.510
Michael actually walks out of the blaze,

00:25:22.510 --> 00:25:24.668
literally covered in burning
flames before finally,

00:25:24.668 --> 00:25:28.000
his body can take him no further
and he falls face forward,

00:25:28.000 --> 00:25:29.060
where he would continue to burn

00:25:29.060 --> 00:25:31.500
until the fire department
arrived, and found him in a coma,

00:25:31.500 --> 00:25:33.040
this time a much more permanent one,

00:25:33.040 --> 00:25:35.770
as he would spend the next 10
years in this comatose state.

00:25:35.770 --> 00:25:38.070
This time, instead of being
taken back to Smith's Grove,

00:25:38.070 --> 00:25:40.300
Michael was locked up in
a higher security facility

00:25:40.300 --> 00:25:42.220
known as Ridgemont Federal Sanitarium,

00:25:42.220 --> 00:25:44.300
where despite being a
vegetable for his entire stay,

00:25:44.300 --> 00:25:46.640
he gained a reputation for
being the devil himself,

00:25:46.640 --> 00:25:48.260
and even the guards are afraid of him.

00:25:48.260 --> 00:25:49.940
As for the room he was locked in...

00:25:49.940 --> 00:25:51.010
- Welcome to hell.

00:25:51.010 --> 00:25:52.720
- After 10 years of being in a coma,

00:25:52.720 --> 00:25:55.020
it doesn't look like Michael
is ever going to come out of it

00:25:55.020 --> 00:25:56.650
and it was decided that
he should be moved back

00:25:56.650 --> 00:25:58.490
to Smith's Grove to
open up space for other

00:25:58.490 --> 00:25:59.750
and more threatening patients.

00:25:59.750 --> 00:26:02.000
Dr. Loomis is still Michael's
doctor during this time,

00:26:02.000 --> 00:26:04.240
though it's said that the
position is more ceremonial.

00:26:04.240 --> 00:26:05.277
Many of the day to day decisions

00:26:05.277 --> 00:26:08.420
fall on the Ridgemont medical
administrator, Dr. Hoffman.

00:26:08.420 --> 00:26:11.420
Michael was to be transferred
on October 30th, 1988,

00:26:11.420 --> 00:26:14.160
one day shy of the 10 year
anniversary of his rampage.

00:26:14.160 --> 00:26:16.700
Extra precautions are taken
to ensure a smooth operation,

00:26:16.700 --> 00:26:19.260
however, disaster strikes
when the ride to Smith's Grove

00:26:19.260 --> 00:26:20.873
doesn't quite go as planned.

00:26:26.010 --> 00:26:28.427
(soft music)

00:26:30.110 --> 00:26:31.790
During Michael Myers' original stay

00:26:31.790 --> 00:26:33.040
at Smith's Grove Sanitarium,

00:26:33.040 --> 00:26:34.790
he was assumed to be relatively harmless

00:26:34.790 --> 00:26:36.330
as more and more time passed.

00:26:36.330 --> 00:26:37.730
He was relatively catatonic,

00:26:37.730 --> 00:26:39.940
and only Dr. Loomis was
able to see through him

00:26:39.940 --> 00:26:41.981
and understand that the
patient was still dangerous.

00:26:41.981 --> 00:26:45.120
It seems that Michael employed
a similar tactic at Ridgemont

00:26:45.120 --> 00:26:47.080
because while it's assumed
he's still comatose

00:26:47.080 --> 00:26:48.190
during his patient transfer,

00:26:48.190 --> 00:26:49.546
he is secretly awake and conscious

00:26:49.546 --> 00:26:53.510
to hear the transfer personnel
discuss his living relatives.

00:26:53.510 --> 00:26:55.522
- Did Hoffman, say anything
about living relatives?

00:26:55.522 --> 00:26:57.790
- Yeah, a niece living in his hometown.

00:26:57.790 --> 00:27:00.860
- Clearly, Michael is sentient
during this ambulance ride.

00:27:00.860 --> 00:27:02.100
It would be hard to say for sure

00:27:02.100 --> 00:27:03.790
how long he's been awake before this,

00:27:03.790 --> 00:27:05.970
but given how he tricked
most of the sanitarium staff

00:27:05.970 --> 00:27:08.630
as a kid, I wouldn't be surprised
if he was faking his coma

00:27:08.630 --> 00:27:10.030
for the last couple years now.

00:27:10.030 --> 00:27:12.180
The information about who
his living relative is

00:27:12.180 --> 00:27:14.540
is also important because
of the Curse of Thorn.

00:27:14.540 --> 00:27:16.170
Even if Laurie wasn't around anymore,

00:27:16.170 --> 00:27:17.990
he still has to take out
the rest of his family

00:27:17.990 --> 00:27:19.910
in order to spare the community at large.

00:27:19.910 --> 00:27:22.310
Once he hears what he needs
to hear, Myers breaks free

00:27:22.310 --> 00:27:24.100
and demonstrates his unbelievable strength

00:27:24.100 --> 00:27:25.870
by shoving his thumb
through the man's forehead

00:27:25.870 --> 00:27:26.760
into his skull.

00:27:26.760 --> 00:27:28.270
They make it just south of Mill Creek,

00:27:28.270 --> 00:27:29.930
about 4 hours outside of Haddonfield,

00:27:29.930 --> 00:27:31.240
before the ambulance crashes,

00:27:31.240 --> 00:27:33.490
probably the result of
Michael attacking the driver.

00:27:33.490 --> 00:27:35.030
It ends up flipped over in a river,

00:27:35.030 --> 00:27:36.330
talk about rolling the ambo,

00:27:36.330 --> 00:27:38.070
but that wasn't even
the end of the suffering

00:27:38.070 --> 00:27:39.810
for at least one of the passengers.

00:27:39.810 --> 00:27:41.030
We can actually see carnage

00:27:41.030 --> 00:27:42.890
smeared all over the
outside of the vehicle,

00:27:42.890 --> 00:27:45.010
which would suggest that one
of the transfer personnel

00:27:45.010 --> 00:27:45.990
actually survived

00:27:45.990 --> 00:27:47.760
and may have tried to
escape the crash site

00:27:47.760 --> 00:27:50.660
only to be reeled back in
and gutted by Michael Myers.

00:27:50.660 --> 00:27:52.470
Since his signature mask and jumpsuit

00:27:52.470 --> 00:27:54.300
burned up in the fire in 1978,

00:27:54.300 --> 00:27:56.040
Michael feels the need
to get back in costume

00:27:56.040 --> 00:27:58.395
and stops at a local auto
shop called Penny's garage.

00:27:58.395 --> 00:28:01.310
Here, he finds a stake and
uses it to impale the mechanic

00:28:01.310 --> 00:28:02.480
and take his jumpsuit.

00:28:02.480 --> 00:28:04.050
He ends up hanging the guy up in chains

00:28:04.050 --> 00:28:05.120
on the back of his tow truck.

00:28:05.120 --> 00:28:06.420
It seems that Michael likes to make

00:28:06.420 --> 00:28:07.690
a spectacle of his victims,

00:28:07.690 --> 00:28:10.230
whether that be the shrine
of babysitters in 1978,

00:28:10.230 --> 00:28:12.540
the unique cause of death for
each of the hospital staff,

00:28:12.540 --> 00:28:15.240
the capsized ambulance, or
now, the strung up mechanic.

00:28:15.240 --> 00:28:17.780
This, like many of his
actions, may go back to Thorn.

00:28:17.780 --> 00:28:19.450
Perhaps Michael wants to show off his work

00:28:19.450 --> 00:28:21.160
to gain favor with the ancient being.

00:28:21.160 --> 00:28:23.260
Or maybe he just does this
to intimidate the survivors

00:28:23.260 --> 00:28:25.340
as much as possible because he enjoys it.

00:28:25.340 --> 00:28:27.440
He goes to the small diner
attached to the garage

00:28:27.440 --> 00:28:29.330
and relieves the waitress of her duties,

00:28:29.330 --> 00:28:31.570
by the looks of it, this
one died by strangulation.

00:28:31.570 --> 00:28:32.480
If you don't like the service,

00:28:32.480 --> 00:28:34.320
you don't have to leave a tip, but damn.

00:28:34.320 --> 00:28:35.990
He also destroys all of the telephones,

00:28:35.990 --> 00:28:37.730
a tactic that worked
well to buy him some time

00:28:37.730 --> 00:28:40.410
before authorities showed
up at the hospital in 1978,

00:28:40.410 --> 00:28:42.020
so why not try it again here?

00:28:42.020 --> 00:28:43.920
It would seem that he is
looking for his next victim

00:28:43.920 --> 00:28:44.753
inside the kitchen,

00:28:44.753 --> 00:28:47.240
when he's confronted by
his old friend, Dr. Loomis.

00:28:47.240 --> 00:28:48.570
His doctor tries to slow him down

00:28:48.570 --> 00:28:49.550
with another round of lead,

00:28:49.550 --> 00:28:50.960
but this time he gets out of the way

00:28:50.960 --> 00:28:52.620
and tries to strand Loomis at the garage

00:28:52.620 --> 00:28:53.770
by stealing a tow truck,

00:28:53.770 --> 00:28:55.320
and using it to sideswipe the gas pump

00:28:55.320 --> 00:28:56.470
to blow up Loomis' car.

00:28:58.470 --> 00:29:00.030
Now that he's got a suit and a vehicle,

00:29:00.030 --> 00:29:01.910
the next item on his
list is getting a mask,

00:29:01.910 --> 00:29:04.450
and he's able to find one at
Vincent Drug in Haddonfield.

00:29:04.450 --> 00:29:06.115
Actually, the one he gets
looks like a cheap knock-off

00:29:06.115 --> 00:29:08.090
of the one he had, which makes sense

00:29:08.090 --> 00:29:10.800
because his actions 10 years
ago made the mask more popular,

00:29:10.800 --> 00:29:13.180
so they had to be
mass-produced at lower quality.

00:29:13.180 --> 00:29:15.920
He also has a chance encounter
with his niece, Jamie Lloyd,

00:29:15.920 --> 00:29:17.780
the living relative that
he heard about earlier,

00:29:17.780 --> 00:29:19.350
but like he did with Laurie in the past,

00:29:19.350 --> 00:29:21.320
he waits until nightfall
to come after her.

00:29:21.320 --> 00:29:22.720
He stalks the house that evening,

00:29:22.720 --> 00:29:24.780
and after Jamie and her
adoptive sister Rachel

00:29:24.780 --> 00:29:25.790
head out for trick-or-treating,

00:29:25.790 --> 00:29:27.100
he does a little investigating

00:29:27.100 --> 00:29:29.201
and confirms Jamie's
relationship to Laurie Strode.

00:29:29.201 --> 00:29:30.760
He also gets his stabbing hand warmed up

00:29:30.760 --> 00:29:33.980
on Rachel and Jamie's dog
because he's an ***hole.

00:29:33.980 --> 00:29:35.390
We know in previous situations

00:29:35.390 --> 00:29:37.250
that Michael has thrived in the darkness,

00:29:37.250 --> 00:29:38.750
like the blackout at the sanitarium,

00:29:38.750 --> 00:29:40.760
and his turning the lights
off in the Wallace house.

00:29:40.760 --> 00:29:42.370
This time, he goes straight to the source,

00:29:42.370 --> 00:29:43.800
the power station in Haddonfield,

00:29:43.800 --> 00:29:45.540
and throws the technician
into a transformer,

00:29:45.540 --> 00:29:46.690
not only electrocuting him,

00:29:46.690 --> 00:29:48.410
but also causing a blackout in town.

00:29:48.410 --> 00:29:50.910
He then completely
massacres the police station

00:29:50.910 --> 00:29:53.180
and leaves the place in ruins
and without a police force,

00:29:53.180 --> 00:29:54.770
save for a couple of stragglers.

00:29:54.770 --> 00:29:56.720
On a foggy backroad, he finds Rachel,

00:29:56.720 --> 00:29:58.610
who is supposed to be
babysitting Jamie that night

00:29:58.610 --> 00:29:59.760
and scares her away.

00:29:59.760 --> 00:30:01.050
At least I assume that's him,

00:30:01.050 --> 00:30:02.970
it's hard to say for sure
with all these imitators

00:30:02.970 --> 00:30:03.803
running around.

00:30:03.803 --> 00:30:05.280
Rachel is soon after
picked up by the police

00:30:05.280 --> 00:30:06.240
with Jamie in tow,

00:30:06.240 --> 00:30:08.660
and again, I assume Michael
is the one who sticks around

00:30:08.660 --> 00:30:09.680
to see where they head.

00:30:09.680 --> 00:30:11.760
However, the car disappears
out of his sight,

00:30:11.760 --> 00:30:13.430
so he breaks into a different police car,

00:30:13.430 --> 00:30:14.880
which is stationed at Jamie's house

00:30:14.880 --> 00:30:17.050
and hides in the back seat
in order to catch a free ride

00:30:17.050 --> 00:30:18.060
to wherever they are going.

00:30:18.060 --> 00:30:19.970
Although the house is
supposedly locked down,

00:30:19.970 --> 00:30:21.740
Michael still finds a way in somehow,

00:30:21.740 --> 00:30:23.710
and eyes his next target, Deputy Logan,

00:30:23.710 --> 00:30:25.350
who is in charge of
guarding the front door.

00:30:25.350 --> 00:30:27.220
Once Loomis and Sheriff
Meeker leave the house,

00:30:27.220 --> 00:30:29.560
he makes his move, literally
tearing his head and hand

00:30:29.560 --> 00:30:30.393
from his body.

00:30:30.393 --> 00:30:32.450
Michael takes a page from
his murder of Bob Simms

00:30:32.450 --> 00:30:34.120
and Linda van der Klok the decade before

00:30:34.120 --> 00:30:35.610
by pretending to someone else.

00:30:35.610 --> 00:30:37.130
He sits in Logan's rocking chair

00:30:37.130 --> 00:30:39.330
until the sheriff's daughter,
Kelly Meeker comes along,

00:30:39.330 --> 00:30:41.390
and in another similarity
to the Bob Simms kill,

00:30:41.390 --> 00:30:42.890
he impales her body up against a door,

00:30:42.890 --> 00:30:45.130
this time using Deputy
Logan's rifle to do so.

00:30:45.130 --> 00:30:47.360
That leaves two more human
obstacles in the house

00:30:47.360 --> 00:30:49.320
for Michael to get through
before reaching Jamie.

00:30:49.320 --> 00:30:51.070
Rachel and her love interest Brady.

00:30:51.070 --> 00:30:52.390
Michael finds them on the stairs

00:30:52.390 --> 00:30:53.880
and Brady tries to fight him physically,

00:30:53.880 --> 00:30:55.140
but is easily no match.

00:30:55.140 --> 00:30:57.100
Michael lifts him up and
crushes his neck and skull

00:30:57.100 --> 00:30:58.110
with his bare hands.

00:30:58.110 --> 00:31:00.560
He conveniently finds another
carving knife in the loft,

00:31:00.560 --> 00:31:02.130
and comes after Rachel and Jamie with it

00:31:02.130 --> 00:31:03.320
onto the roof of the house,

00:31:03.320 --> 00:31:05.280
where he narrowly misses
turning the elder of the two

00:31:05.280 --> 00:31:07.290
into a rooftop Halloween decoration.

00:31:07.290 --> 00:31:09.070
He eventually knocks
her down onto the lawn

00:31:09.070 --> 00:31:11.680
where she falls unconscious,
but Jamie is able to escape.

00:31:11.680 --> 00:31:13.670
However, Michael hears the
security alarm going off

00:31:13.670 --> 00:31:14.800
in the elementary school,

00:31:14.800 --> 00:31:16.410
and decides to search there for her.

00:31:16.410 --> 00:31:17.868
Suddenly having blond
hair for some reason,

00:31:17.868 --> 00:31:20.207
he ambushes Dr. Loomis and
throws him out of the way,

00:31:20.207 --> 00:31:21.640
and he goes flying through the door

00:31:21.640 --> 00:31:23.590
like a doberman through a coffee table.

00:31:25.020 --> 00:31:26.870
Michael, after quickly
popping into the bathroom

00:31:26.870 --> 00:31:27.910
to dye his hair back to normal,

00:31:27.910 --> 00:31:29.690
appears on the stairs behind Jamie,

00:31:29.690 --> 00:31:31.050
and he's actually able to grab her

00:31:31.050 --> 00:31:32.340
after she falls down the steps

00:31:32.340 --> 00:31:33.980
and is unable to get back on her feet.

00:31:33.980 --> 00:31:35.340
However, Rachel saves her

00:31:35.340 --> 00:31:36.650
when she shows up to blind Michael

00:31:36.650 --> 00:31:38.600
with a fire extinguisher
sprayed in his face.

00:31:38.600 --> 00:31:40.240
If Malcolm in the Middle
is to be believed,

00:31:40.240 --> 00:31:41.600
this could actually work.

00:31:41.600 --> 00:31:43.640
However, as per usual with Michael Myers,

00:31:43.640 --> 00:31:45.400
his blindness is only temporary,

00:31:45.400 --> 00:31:47.200
and he's actually able
to sneak past everybody

00:31:47.200 --> 00:31:48.900
and latch himself onto
the bottom of the truck

00:31:48.900 --> 00:31:50.540
that comes to rescue Rachel and Jamie.

00:31:50.540 --> 00:31:52.920
He clings to it as it
b-lines out of Haddonfield.

00:31:52.920 --> 00:31:55.060
Anyone who's ever had to do
the arm hang in gym class

00:31:55.060 --> 00:31:56.706
knows how much strength this requires.

00:31:56.706 --> 00:31:58.350
I think I could handle it though.

00:31:58.350 --> 00:32:00.160
He climbs up while the car is in motion

00:32:00.160 --> 00:32:01.660
and defeats all three of the Illinois boys

00:32:01.660 --> 00:32:03.850
riding in the back before
punching through the window

00:32:03.850 --> 00:32:05.490
to tear off the face of the driver.

00:32:05.490 --> 00:32:07.320
Rachel takes the wheel
and tries to buck him off

00:32:07.320 --> 00:32:09.020
with some sharp turns, but
when that doesn't work,

00:32:09.020 --> 00:32:10.730
she resorts to slamming the brakes.

00:32:10.730 --> 00:32:13.677
Vocabulary time, I'm gonna
call that a brake yeet.

00:32:13.677 --> 00:32:15.350
(tires screeching)

00:32:15.350 --> 00:32:16.945
Michael gets up looking
ready to line up and block

00:32:16.945 --> 00:32:18.550
for the Chicago Bears offense,

00:32:18.550 --> 00:32:20.440
so Rachel just channels
her inner linebacker

00:32:20.440 --> 00:32:21.570
and tries to run him over,

00:32:21.570 --> 00:32:23.890
and since this would be a fatal
blow for any normal human,

00:32:23.890 --> 00:32:26.040
it knocks him unconscious
for a period of time.

00:32:26.040 --> 00:32:28.250
A confused Jamie wanders
into the roadside ditch

00:32:28.250 --> 00:32:30.380
that Michael is lying
in and grabs his hand.

00:32:30.380 --> 00:32:32.060
It's my understanding that this action

00:32:32.060 --> 00:32:34.100
causes a mental connection
between the two,

00:32:34.100 --> 00:32:36.847
that he was transferring
part of his curse onto her.

00:32:42.539 --> 00:32:45.039
(eerie music)

00:32:46.600 --> 00:32:48.740
After being rammed into a roadside ditch

00:32:48.740 --> 00:32:50.350
with the full force of a pickup truck,

00:32:50.350 --> 00:32:51.362
the life comes back into Michael

00:32:51.362 --> 00:32:53.680
just a moment too late to attack Jamie,

00:32:53.680 --> 00:32:55.726
and instead, the police and
the remaining Illinois boys

00:32:55.726 --> 00:32:57.430
all open fire on him.

00:32:57.430 --> 00:32:59.190
With seven men all firing shots,

00:32:59.190 --> 00:33:01.010
Michael is knocked back into a hole.

00:33:01.010 --> 00:33:03.910
Michael Myers is not usually
one to back away from a fight,

00:33:03.910 --> 00:33:06.320
but I think this time he
realizes he's overmatched,

00:33:06.320 --> 00:33:07.530
and not wanting to end back up

00:33:07.530 --> 00:33:09.080
in a high security mental hospital,

00:33:09.080 --> 00:33:11.390
he crawls away and finds an
opening to wiggle through

00:33:11.390 --> 00:33:12.320
just before the police

00:33:12.320 --> 00:33:13.870
drop a stick of dynamite into the hole

00:33:13.870 --> 00:33:15.150
to try to finish him off.

00:33:15.150 --> 00:33:17.370
He ends up floating down a
stream to quickly get away

00:33:17.370 --> 00:33:18.770
and ends up at a homeless camp,

00:33:18.770 --> 00:33:20.030
and when it's scruffy inhabitant

00:33:20.030 --> 00:33:22.963
comes out to investigate the
disturbance, this happens.

00:33:27.050 --> 00:33:29.060
I'm guessing Michael
just runs out of energy.

00:33:29.060 --> 00:33:30.750
I think it's been well
established at this point

00:33:30.750 --> 00:33:32.200
that whenever Michael survives death,

00:33:32.200 --> 00:33:34.070
he needs some time to
regenerate his power,

00:33:34.070 --> 00:33:35.250
to recharge himself.

00:33:35.250 --> 00:33:36.500
We saw him take a quick rest

00:33:36.500 --> 00:33:37.980
after being struck by the pickup truck,

00:33:37.980 --> 00:33:40.440
but he never recharges after
being shot up by the gunmen,

00:33:40.440 --> 00:33:42.390
because he needs to use a
little more of his energy

00:33:42.390 --> 00:33:44.210
to get out of there before
the dynamite goes off

00:33:44.210 --> 00:33:45.740
and puts him in another coma.

00:33:45.740 --> 00:33:47.212
It's just back at the
hospital 10 years ago.

00:33:47.212 --> 00:33:49.940
After the explosion, he's able
to go on a little bit longer

00:33:49.940 --> 00:33:51.760
if he really puts in some extra effort.

00:33:51.760 --> 00:33:53.900
So Michael was essentially
just delaying the inevitable,

00:33:53.900 --> 00:33:54.790
and he runs out of power

00:33:54.790 --> 00:33:56.650
once he gets some
distance from the police.

00:33:56.650 --> 00:33:58.730
It's not clear what happens
directly after that,

00:33:58.730 --> 00:34:00.390
but Michael would
continue to hide out there

00:34:00.390 --> 00:34:01.340
for an entire year,

00:34:01.340 --> 00:34:03.400
once again using the days
surrounding Halloween

00:34:03.400 --> 00:34:05.370
as the time frame for his violent ritual.

00:34:05.370 --> 00:34:07.310
It was October 30th, 1989,

00:34:07.310 --> 00:34:08.430
when he finally took the knife

00:34:08.430 --> 00:34:10.030
to his off-the-grid co-habitant,

00:34:10.030 --> 00:34:11.280
not the nicest way to treat a guy

00:34:11.280 --> 00:34:13.000
who gave you a free
place to live for a year,

00:34:13.000 --> 00:34:15.030
but I guess at this point
you've probably realized

00:34:15.030 --> 00:34:17.100
that Michael is not the nicest guy.

00:34:17.100 --> 00:34:19.260
The next day he hides outside
of the Carruthers's home,

00:34:19.260 --> 00:34:21.050
then breaks in the back
and spies on Rachel

00:34:21.050 --> 00:34:22.500
as she gets herself ready to go out.

00:34:22.500 --> 00:34:24.120
After ****ing around in
the house for a while,

00:34:24.120 --> 00:34:25.560
he decides he's waited long enough,

00:34:25.560 --> 00:34:27.630
and gets her with a pair of
scissors through the chest.

00:34:27.630 --> 00:34:29.170
Rachel, like many of the victims

00:34:29.170 --> 00:34:30.470
that Michael took out this Halloween,

00:34:30.470 --> 00:34:32.310
is deposited into a
shrine that he's building

00:34:32.310 --> 00:34:33.640
in the attic of the Myers House,

00:34:33.640 --> 00:34:35.422
I already talked about how
Michael loves his shrines.

00:34:35.422 --> 00:34:37.490
Later, Rachel's friends, Tina and Sammy,

00:34:37.490 --> 00:34:38.360
come over to look for her,

00:34:38.360 --> 00:34:40.430
so Michael decides to stalk
them for a little while.

00:34:40.430 --> 00:34:42.320
Michael's just trying to
relive the good old days.

00:34:42.320 --> 00:34:43.930
Back then it was teenage babysitters,

00:34:43.930 --> 00:34:46.050
now it's teenage housesitters;
he'll take what he can get.

00:34:46.050 --> 00:34:47.729
The next victim of that year's Halloween

00:34:47.729 --> 00:34:49.530
is Tina's boyfriend, Mikey.

00:34:49.530 --> 00:34:50.930
Mike-ULL gets a rise out of him

00:34:50.930 --> 00:34:52.290
by leaving a scratch on his fancy car.

00:34:52.290 --> 00:34:54.130
When Mik-EY tries to
start a fight over it,

00:34:54.130 --> 00:34:56.190
he stops him in his tracks
by grabbing his throat,

00:34:56.190 --> 00:34:58.910
and whacks him with what
looks to be a gardening fork.

00:34:58.910 --> 00:34:59.980
Keeping up with the tradition

00:34:59.980 --> 00:35:02.120
of pretending to be someone
else, he steals Mikey's car

00:35:02.120 --> 00:35:03.630
and wears the mask that Tina got him.

00:35:03.630 --> 00:35:04.660
She gets into the car

00:35:04.660 --> 00:35:06.380
thinking that she's being
picked up by her boyfriend

00:35:06.380 --> 00:35:07.440
to go to the Halloween party.

00:35:07.440 --> 00:35:10.030
- I just love Barbaric men.

00:35:10.030 --> 00:35:11.310
- You'll love this guy, Tina.

00:35:11.310 --> 00:35:12.791
I also love how when
Tina tries to kiss him,

00:35:12.791 --> 00:35:14.980
he just takes it, and then looks at her.

00:35:14.980 --> 00:35:16.580
It's even weirder when
you think about the fact

00:35:16.580 --> 00:35:18.270
that that's his first kiss.

00:35:18.270 --> 00:35:20.000
She asks if they can stop
for a pack of cigarettes,

00:35:20.000 --> 00:35:22.320
so he stops at a gas station,
and while she's inside,

00:35:22.320 --> 00:35:23.153
he switches back

00:35:23.153 --> 00:35:26.290
into his usual William
Shatner/Greg Nicotero looking mask,

00:35:26.290 --> 00:35:28.120
a sign that he was
probably about to give her

00:35:28.120 --> 00:35:29.660
the old Michael Myers special.

00:35:29.660 --> 00:35:31.840
I am really running out of
advertiser-friendly ways

00:35:31.840 --> 00:35:33.730
to say that Michael Myers
killed someone, okay?

00:35:33.730 --> 00:35:35.470
However, before she gets back in the car,

00:35:35.470 --> 00:35:37.530
the police raid the gas
station and pick her up.

00:35:37.530 --> 00:35:39.130
They had been tipped off
that she was in danger

00:35:39.130 --> 00:35:40.780
thanks in part to Jamie's psychic vision,

00:35:40.780 --> 00:35:42.880
and Michael, the real
Michael Myers, that is,

00:35:42.880 --> 00:35:43.730
flees the area.

00:35:43.730 --> 00:35:45.100
We see this iteration of Michael Myers

00:35:45.100 --> 00:35:47.420
start to shy away from crowds
of armed police officers,

00:35:47.420 --> 00:35:48.640
because he knows what can happen

00:35:48.640 --> 00:35:49.570
if he gets shot too many times,

00:35:49.570 --> 00:35:51.270
he'll have to do his recharge thing,

00:35:51.270 --> 00:35:52.860
and that gives authorities an opportunity

00:35:52.860 --> 00:35:54.010
to potentially pick him up,

00:35:54.010 --> 00:35:55.810
and he wants to avoid
going back to Smith's Grove

00:35:55.810 --> 00:35:57.720
or any other facility at all costs.

00:35:57.720 --> 00:35:59.820
Later that night, he shows
up at The Tower Farm,

00:35:59.820 --> 00:36:01.640
which is home to the
biggest teen Halloween party

00:36:01.640 --> 00:36:02.473
in Haddonfield.

00:36:02.473 --> 00:36:04.810
He sees Tina, Sammy, and
Sammy's boyfriend, Spitz,

00:36:04.810 --> 00:36:06.870
leave the party and go
into the barn next door.

00:36:06.870 --> 00:36:08.590
Michael equips himself with a pitchfork,

00:36:08.590 --> 00:36:11.870
and pitches Spitz out of the
way before grabbing a scythe

00:36:11.870 --> 00:36:13.640
and harvesting Sammy's neck.

00:36:13.640 --> 00:36:14.700
When he comes out of the barn,

00:36:14.700 --> 00:36:17.070
his local infamy actually
works to his advantage,

00:36:17.070 --> 00:36:18.000
because the cops assume

00:36:18.000 --> 00:36:19.610
that he's just a kid that they saw earlier

00:36:19.610 --> 00:36:21.190
who was dressed up as Michael Myers.

00:36:21.190 --> 00:36:24.180
I can understand why a lot of
kids dressed up as him in 1988

00:36:24.180 --> 00:36:25.140
during Halloween 4,

00:36:25.140 --> 00:36:27.400
because it had been 10 years
since the babysitter massacre

00:36:27.400 --> 00:36:30.160
at that point, but dressing
up as Michael in 1989,

00:36:30.160 --> 00:36:32.960
in Haddonfield, when 17
people lost their lives to him

00:36:32.960 --> 00:36:33.830
the prior Fall,

00:36:33.830 --> 00:36:35.940
and he's still a wanted
criminal on the loose

00:36:35.940 --> 00:36:37.570
and most certainly somewhere in town

00:36:37.570 --> 00:36:38.550
because it's Halloween?

00:36:38.550 --> 00:36:40.573
Maybe that's just not the smartest move.

00:36:40.573 --> 00:36:42.140
But anyway, with their guard down,

00:36:42.140 --> 00:36:44.500
he's easily able to take out
the cops with the pitchfork.

00:36:44.500 --> 00:36:46.900
He gets back in the car, maybe
planning to go find Jamie,

00:36:46.900 --> 00:36:48.260
when Jamie just shows up on the scene

00:36:48.260 --> 00:36:49.490
with her little friend Billy.

00:36:49.490 --> 00:36:51.540
This boogeyman business
is getting way too easy,

00:36:51.540 --> 00:36:53.360
the victims are supposed
to run away from him,

00:36:53.360 --> 00:36:54.760
not the other way around.

00:36:54.760 --> 00:36:56.160
He starts by chasing down Tina

00:36:56.160 --> 00:36:58.360
by intentionally driving slowly after her.

00:36:58.360 --> 00:36:59.540
Jimmy and I talked about this

00:36:59.540 --> 00:37:00.860
in the Halloween 5 Things You Missed.

00:37:00.860 --> 00:37:03.200
Everyone knows that
Michael Myers walks slow.

00:37:03.200 --> 00:37:04.890
We're never given a
concrete reason for this,

00:37:04.890 --> 00:37:07.260
but I've always assumed
that it ties into his curse.

00:37:07.260 --> 00:37:08.948
I talked about how he
spent his first 15 years

00:37:08.948 --> 00:37:10.990
in Smith's Grove in near-catatonia.

00:37:10.990 --> 00:37:13.820
He became known for being
this creepy, unmoving shape.

00:37:13.820 --> 00:37:15.819
So he kept that aspect
of his persona in tact

00:37:15.819 --> 00:37:18.620
by chasing his victims at
a slow and steady rate,

00:37:18.620 --> 00:37:20.350
relying more on power than speed.

00:37:20.350 --> 00:37:22.330
It doesn't often end up
being a detriment to him,

00:37:22.330 --> 00:37:24.840
because his victims are usually
distracted, fear-stricken,

00:37:24.840 --> 00:37:26.180
or stupidly brave,

00:37:26.180 --> 00:37:27.800
so it's not often that somebody gets away.

00:37:27.800 --> 00:37:31.110
But seeing Michael go after
someone slowly in a car

00:37:31.110 --> 00:37:32.600
doesn't make a whole lot of sense,

00:37:32.600 --> 00:37:34.100
since we've seen in previous scenes

00:37:34.100 --> 00:37:36.170
that he is capable of driving fast.

00:37:36.170 --> 00:37:37.920
The only explanation that makes sense here

00:37:37.920 --> 00:37:39.760
is that Michael is savoring his kill,

00:37:39.760 --> 00:37:41.340
he's intentionally stretching it out

00:37:41.340 --> 00:37:42.870
because he enjoys being the predator,

00:37:42.870 --> 00:37:45.023
and maybe enjoys seeing the
fear on his victims' faces

00:37:45.023 --> 00:37:46.699
and in their body language.

00:37:46.699 --> 00:37:49.240
(Tina screams)

00:37:49.240 --> 00:37:50.546
- [Zac] Maybe this is also why Michael

00:37:50.546 --> 00:37:52.560
intentionally misses Laurie with a knife

00:37:52.560 --> 00:37:55.160
so many times on that
night in '78, who knows?

00:37:55.160 --> 00:37:56.890
Before reaching Tina, he changes course

00:37:56.890 --> 00:37:58.320
and comes after Jamie and Billy.

00:37:58.320 --> 00:37:59.320
Reasoning for this?

00:37:59.320 --> 00:38:01.120
I think maybe he didn't
see them right away?

00:38:01.120 --> 00:38:03.230
It's pretty hard to do a
character analysis video

00:38:03.230 --> 00:38:05.040
on someone who has so little character,

00:38:05.040 --> 00:38:06.850
but that's also what makes him great.

00:38:06.850 --> 00:38:08.470
Jamie zig-zags her way into the woods,

00:38:08.470 --> 00:38:10.650
which results in Michael
crashing the car into a tree,

00:38:10.650 --> 00:38:12.693
and somehow it explodes.

00:38:17.010 --> 00:38:19.700
Tina's boyfriend would be
pissed if he were still alive.

00:38:19.700 --> 00:38:21.710
Michael continues to pursue Jamie on foot,

00:38:21.710 --> 00:38:23.010
and due to her injured leg,

00:38:23.010 --> 00:38:25.610
it looks like he might get her
until Tina sacrifices herself

00:38:25.610 --> 00:38:26.970
to give Jamie more time.

00:38:26.970 --> 00:38:28.550
Michael uses the knife for this one,

00:38:28.550 --> 00:38:30.500
a true classic never goes out of style.

00:38:31.370 --> 00:38:33.010
Wait, wrong franchise.

00:38:33.010 --> 00:38:34.870
That's when the rest of
the police force shows up

00:38:34.870 --> 00:38:36.050
to rescue Jamie and Billy,

00:38:36.050 --> 00:38:37.830
and after they're safely escorted away,

00:38:37.830 --> 00:38:39.840
Loomis meets Michael at
the edge of the forest

00:38:39.840 --> 00:38:40.673
with a message.

00:38:40.673 --> 00:38:42.450
He tells Michael that
the rage that drives him

00:38:42.450 --> 00:38:44.080
will not go away if he kills everyone,

00:38:44.080 --> 00:38:45.310
the only way he can get rid of it

00:38:45.310 --> 00:38:46.930
is to face it where it first began,

00:38:46.930 --> 00:38:49.000
his childhood home on Lampkin Lane.

00:38:49.000 --> 00:38:51.410
This is the first time we've
ever seen an internal struggle

00:38:51.410 --> 00:38:52.330
inside of Michael.

00:38:52.330 --> 00:38:53.980
For the last 26 years of his life,

00:38:53.980 --> 00:38:55.930
he's been consumed by this Curse of Thorn.

00:38:55.930 --> 00:38:57.950
All of his actions have
been motivated by it.

00:38:57.950 --> 00:38:59.220
For the first time since then,

00:38:59.220 --> 00:39:02.513
we would see the real Michael
Myers creeping to the surface.

00:39:08.004 --> 00:39:11.160
(eerie music)

00:39:11.160 --> 00:39:12.950
Before heading home to the Myers House,

00:39:12.950 --> 00:39:14.190
Michael first makes an appearance

00:39:14.190 --> 00:39:15.770
at the Haddonfield Children's Clinic.

00:39:15.770 --> 00:39:17.280
This is where Jamie and Billy live.

00:39:17.280 --> 00:39:18.810
This accomplishes a few things.

00:39:18.810 --> 00:39:21.300
One, Michael is able to
determine that Jamie isn't there,

00:39:21.300 --> 00:39:23.653
as promised by Loomis who is
with her at the Myers House.

00:39:23.653 --> 00:39:25.580
Two, it draws the police
in that direction,

00:39:25.580 --> 00:39:28.010
making it easier for Michael
to get back into his old home.

00:39:28.010 --> 00:39:29.850
And three, he attacks one of the officers

00:39:29.850 --> 00:39:31.660
guarding the clinic and
steals his squad car,

00:39:31.660 --> 00:39:33.730
which he uses to drive
himself to Lamkin Lane

00:39:33.730 --> 00:39:36.190
and rear end the only cop
still defending the perimeter,

00:39:36.190 --> 00:39:38.640
shortly before smashing his
face in on the dashboard.

00:39:38.640 --> 00:39:41.230
He makes his way inside, and
Loomis meets him downstairs

00:39:41.230 --> 00:39:42.920
and tries to convince him
to put down the knife,

00:39:42.920 --> 00:39:44.320
telling him that Jamie is the key

00:39:44.320 --> 00:39:46.250
to putting an end to
the rage inside of him.

00:39:46.250 --> 00:39:48.860
Michael actually hesitates
and lowers the knife at first,

00:39:48.860 --> 00:39:50.950
and for a moment, it looks
as if his psychiatrist

00:39:50.950 --> 00:39:52.330
is finally getting through to him.

00:39:52.330 --> 00:39:54.460
This shows that the human
side of Michael Myers

00:39:54.460 --> 00:39:55.830
is still down there somewhere,

00:39:55.830 --> 00:39:57.340
and although we don't see it often,

00:39:57.340 --> 00:39:59.120
he does want to escape the malediction

00:39:59.120 --> 00:40:00.550
that's been inflicted upon him.

00:40:00.550 --> 00:40:02.610
It seems that the rage wins
over in the end though,

00:40:02.610 --> 00:40:03.603
because he comes to his senses

00:40:03.603 --> 00:40:05.870
and slashes Dr. Loomis across the torso,

00:40:05.870 --> 00:40:07.640
then tosses him down the stairs.

00:40:07.640 --> 00:40:09.560
Michael goes after Jamie,
but she scurries away,

00:40:09.560 --> 00:40:12.030
so he gets his fix by tying
a rope around this cop's neck

00:40:12.030 --> 00:40:13.260
and tossing him out the window.

00:40:13.260 --> 00:40:16.160
Michael chases Jamie downstairs,
then down to the basement,

00:40:16.160 --> 00:40:18.050
then upstairs, then up to the attic.

00:40:18.050 --> 00:40:20.440
Jamie discovers what happened
to Rachel and her dog Max,

00:40:20.440 --> 00:40:21.740
and in a last ditch effort,

00:40:21.740 --> 00:40:23.770
lies down inside the coffin
that Michael has setup for her

00:40:23.770 --> 00:40:25.770
and attempts to have a heart
to heart with her Uncle.

00:40:25.770 --> 00:40:28.240
Surprisingly, Jamie is
actually able to get through

00:40:28.240 --> 00:40:29.820
to the human side of Michael Myers

00:40:29.820 --> 00:40:32.110
in a way that Dr. Loomis
was never able to.

00:40:32.110 --> 00:40:34.340
She asks him to take off
his mask and when he does,

00:40:34.340 --> 00:40:36.350
Jamie sees a tear running down his face.

00:40:36.350 --> 00:40:38.066
She even comments on his humanity.

00:40:38.066 --> 00:40:40.137
- You're just like me.

00:40:40.137 --> 00:40:42.193
- I'm an ***hole just like you.
- Hmm.

00:40:45.550 --> 00:40:47.870
- However, Michael's moment
of humanity peeking through

00:40:47.870 --> 00:40:50.470
is short lived, when Jamie
tries to wipe away his tears

00:40:50.470 --> 00:40:51.980
and the rage takes back over.

00:40:51.980 --> 00:40:54.620
She runs downstairs, and when
Michael comes down to find her

00:40:54.620 --> 00:40:57.860
he finds Dr. Loomis offering her to him?

00:40:57.860 --> 00:41:00.080
This must have been a
surprising turn of events.

00:41:00.080 --> 00:41:01.960
It would be like if Susan
just showed up at my door

00:41:01.960 --> 00:41:03.810
and handed me the gold creator award.

00:41:03.810 --> 00:41:05.348
Of course, it turns out to be a trap,

00:41:05.348 --> 00:41:06.960
which if Susan shows up at my door,

00:41:06.960 --> 00:41:09.100
I'm definitely gonna assume it's a trap.

00:41:09.100 --> 00:41:11.010
- Shut that door.

00:41:11.010 --> 00:41:13.180
- [Zac] A large net of heavy
metal chains falls from above,

00:41:13.180 --> 00:41:14.800
considerably slowing down his movement

00:41:14.800 --> 00:41:16.880
as he loads Michael up
with tranquilizer darts,

00:41:16.880 --> 00:41:18.683
then just goes to town with a plank.

00:41:22.751 --> 00:41:27.746
- Die! Die! Die! Die! Michael!

00:41:30.256 --> 00:41:31.089
Die!

00:41:35.369 --> 00:41:36.590
Die!

00:41:36.590 --> 00:41:37.881
- Yeah.

00:41:39.023 --> 00:41:40.022
Michael wakes up in jail,

00:41:40.022 --> 00:41:42.350
but this time his stay in
captivity wouldn't last long,

00:41:42.350 --> 00:41:44.880
as Dr. Wynn decided to take
matters into his own hands

00:41:44.880 --> 00:41:47.400
to make sure his protege
lives up to expectations.

00:41:47.400 --> 00:41:49.440
Wynn single-handedly
raids the police station.

00:41:49.440 --> 00:41:51.730
He makes quick work of the
seven officers stationed there

00:41:51.730 --> 00:41:53.210
and blows the door off of Michael's cell

00:41:53.210 --> 00:41:54.740
where the two can make a quick getaway.

00:41:54.740 --> 00:41:56.930
Despite being free again, it
would be a number of years

00:41:56.930 --> 00:41:58.350
before the planets aligned properly

00:41:58.350 --> 00:42:00.230
for Michael to make his next Samhain--

00:42:00.230 --> 00:42:02.183
- [Loomis] Sam Hain.
- Sacrifice.

00:42:03.860 --> 00:42:06.570
Now if you're riding along with
us on the Halloween Express,

00:42:06.570 --> 00:42:08.040
we've just finished Halloween 5

00:42:08.040 --> 00:42:10.240
and we're moving on to The
Curse of Michael Myers.

00:42:10.240 --> 00:42:11.810
There are two versions of this movie,

00:42:11.810 --> 00:42:13.660
the Theatrical Cut and the Producer's Cut,

00:42:13.660 --> 00:42:15.220
which was publicly released later.

00:42:15.220 --> 00:42:16.670
They're basically the same movie,

00:42:16.670 --> 00:42:18.220
the biggest difference is the endings,

00:42:18.220 --> 00:42:20.020
which is why you'll ride
all the way into the station

00:42:20.020 --> 00:42:21.760
with us no matter which one you choose,

00:42:21.760 --> 00:42:23.430
and your decision will only really dictate

00:42:23.430 --> 00:42:25.060
which platform you exit to.

00:42:25.060 --> 00:42:26.850
The Theatrical Cut is technically canon,

00:42:26.850 --> 00:42:28.440
so that's the direction
I'll be heading in,

00:42:28.440 --> 00:42:30.310
but if you wanna see me talk
about the Producer's Cut,

00:42:30.310 --> 00:42:31.890
check out the Things You Missed episode.

00:42:31.890 --> 00:42:34.430
It's been six years since
Michael escaped the jail cell,

00:42:34.430 --> 00:42:36.620
leading many to speculate
on if he is dead or alive.

00:42:36.620 --> 00:42:38.820
It is October 30th, 1995,

00:42:38.820 --> 00:42:41.060
and Jamie Lloyd is pregnant
with her first child.

00:42:41.060 --> 00:42:42.500
She's kidnapped by the Cult of Thorn

00:42:42.500 --> 00:42:43.650
shortly before the delivery

00:42:43.650 --> 00:42:45.550
so that they can pass
the curse onto the baby

00:42:45.550 --> 00:42:47.070
or let Michael kill both of them,

00:42:47.070 --> 00:42:49.590
but a nice nurse helps her
escape with her first born.

00:42:49.590 --> 00:42:51.510
After six years of waiting in the shadows,

00:42:51.510 --> 00:42:53.260
Michael is dispatched to stop them.

00:42:53.260 --> 00:42:54.880
He pins the helpful nurse up on a wall,

00:42:54.880 --> 00:42:57.110
completing his trilogy
of wall-art victims,

00:42:57.110 --> 00:42:58.560
and snaps the neck of a random guy

00:42:58.560 --> 00:42:59.920
who gets in between him and Jamie,

00:42:59.920 --> 00:43:01.780
but she manages to get away in a vehicle.

00:43:01.780 --> 00:43:03.630
Michael uses a Smith's
Grove van to hunt her

00:43:03.630 --> 00:43:05.600
and runs her off the road
into a pumpkin patch.

00:43:05.600 --> 00:43:07.450
She attempts to hide inside
of the adjacent barn,

00:43:07.450 --> 00:43:09.330
but having just delivered a baby that day,

00:43:09.330 --> 00:43:11.420
there's not much more
energy or fight in her,

00:43:11.420 --> 00:43:12.820
and after seven years of waiting,

00:43:12.820 --> 00:43:15.070
Michael finally brings
his niece's life to an end

00:43:15.070 --> 00:43:16.590
by picking her up and skewering her

00:43:16.590 --> 00:43:18.120
on this piece of farming equipment.

00:43:18.120 --> 00:43:20.110
It seems like she's already
done for at this point,

00:43:20.110 --> 00:43:21.110
but just to make sure,

00:43:21.110 --> 00:43:23.540
he proceeds to turn on
said farming equipment.

00:43:23.540 --> 00:43:24.854
For the first time in 32 years,

00:43:24.854 --> 00:43:27.670
he actually managed to make
some progress on his main goal,

00:43:27.670 --> 00:43:29.370
which is sacrificing his family members.

00:43:29.370 --> 00:43:30.450
Unfortunately for him,

00:43:30.450 --> 00:43:32.600
he cannot be freed from
his curse just yet,

00:43:32.600 --> 00:43:34.880
because now he has Jamie's
baby to track down.

00:43:34.880 --> 00:43:37.915
- [Loomis] She is the
last of his bloodline.

00:43:37.915 --> 00:43:39.840
- [Tommy] No Dr. Loomis.

00:43:39.840 --> 00:43:41.210
She's not the last.

00:43:41.210 --> 00:43:44.760
- [Zac] The next day is
Halloween, October 31st, 1995.

00:43:44.760 --> 00:43:47.000
Just as he always does when
he returns to Haddonfield,

00:43:47.000 --> 00:43:48.430
Michael visits his childhood home,

00:43:48.430 --> 00:43:50.870
but this time he finds
another family living there.

00:43:50.870 --> 00:43:52.010
This is the Strode family,

00:43:52.010 --> 00:43:53.890
the relatives of the
couple that adopted Laurie

00:43:53.890 --> 00:43:55.000
all those years ago.

00:43:55.000 --> 00:43:56.960
Naturally, Michael is not anymore a fan

00:43:56.960 --> 00:43:57.903
of someone else living in his old room

00:43:57.903 --> 00:43:59.610
than he was 17 years ago,

00:43:59.610 --> 00:44:01.065
so he deals with these negative emotions

00:44:01.065 --> 00:44:03.470
the same way he deals
with everything in life,

00:44:03.470 --> 00:44:04.350
by killing them.

00:44:04.350 --> 00:44:06.660
The mother, Debra Strode
gets cut down with an axe,

00:44:06.660 --> 00:44:08.360
but Michael, in maybe the nicest thing

00:44:08.360 --> 00:44:09.430
he's ever done for anyone,

00:44:09.430 --> 00:44:11.420
is courteous enough to
put her stuff in the wash.

00:44:11.420 --> 00:44:13.890
It looks like she had spilled
some cherry slurpee on it.

00:44:13.890 --> 00:44:16.280
The father, John Strode, is
thrown into a breaker box

00:44:16.280 --> 00:44:17.113
and electrocuted.

00:44:17.113 --> 00:44:21.163
Like Mikey's car six years
before, he inexplicably explodes?

00:44:23.540 --> 00:44:25.790
John and Debra's son Tim
and his girlfriend Beth

00:44:25.790 --> 00:44:26.740
are at the live airing

00:44:26.740 --> 00:44:28.720
of a Haddonfield Halloween radio special.

00:44:28.720 --> 00:44:31.380
Michael goes there and ambushes
the host inside of his van.

00:44:31.380 --> 00:44:32.870
The body would later fall out of a tree,

00:44:32.870 --> 00:44:34.250
terrifying the spectators.

00:44:34.250 --> 00:44:36.470
Later still, he returns
home, where Tim and Beth

00:44:36.470 --> 00:44:37.920
are already getting hot and heavy.

00:44:37.920 --> 00:44:39.310
Tim jumps in the shower afterwards

00:44:39.310 --> 00:44:40.670
and asks Beth to bring him a towel,

00:44:40.670 --> 00:44:42.310
but Michael brings one instead.

00:44:42.310 --> 00:44:44.700
Tim doesn't notice the thorn
symbol on his wrist though,

00:44:44.700 --> 00:44:47.240
so Michael gives him the old
throat slash when he gets out,

00:44:47.240 --> 00:44:49.000
then proceeds to stab Beth in the back.

00:44:49.000 --> 00:44:53.750
In the theatrical cut, the
edit is very YouTube Poop-ish.

00:44:56.188 --> 00:44:57.021
[Ganon] Die!

00:44:58.261 --> 00:45:01.952
(ominious music)

00:45:03.480 --> 00:45:05.730
That just leaves John and
Debra's daughter, Kara Strode,

00:45:05.730 --> 00:45:08.520
and her son Danny as the last
two inhabitants of the house.

00:45:08.520 --> 00:45:10.320
Kara manages to hide in a dark corner

00:45:10.320 --> 00:45:11.780
and knock Michael down the stairs,

00:45:11.780 --> 00:45:13.740
making her the first
one to knock Michael out

00:45:13.740 --> 00:45:14.840
with her bare hands.

00:45:14.840 --> 00:45:16.290
He comes back and grabs her ankle

00:45:16.290 --> 00:45:17.830
as she's trying to get
Danny to safety though,

00:45:17.830 --> 00:45:20.640
and she's only able to escape by
whacking him with a fire poker.

00:45:20.640 --> 00:45:22.810
He chases them back across the
street to the boarding house,

00:45:22.810 --> 00:45:24.440
but Dr. Wynn and the other cult members

00:45:24.440 --> 00:45:25.280
are waiting for them there,

00:45:25.280 --> 00:45:26.360
so Michael is instructed

00:45:26.360 --> 00:45:27.980
to return to his home away from home,

00:45:27.980 --> 00:45:29.823
The Smith's Grove Sanitarium.

00:45:34.868 --> 00:45:37.451
(upbeat music)

00:45:38.920 --> 00:45:40.730
That brings us to the last morning

00:45:40.730 --> 00:45:44.750
of the original Halloween
timeline, November 1st, 1995.

00:45:44.750 --> 00:45:47.480
November 1st is one of the
worst days of the year as it is,

00:45:47.480 --> 00:45:49.190
because it's the furthest
day from Halloween

00:45:49.190 --> 00:45:50.023
on the calendar.

00:45:50.023 --> 00:45:52.370
I can only imagine that having
an immortal serial killer

00:45:52.370 --> 00:45:55.190
after you on that day doesn't
make it any easier to swallow.

00:45:55.190 --> 00:45:57.090
Jamie's baby, who's been
named Stephen Strode,

00:45:57.090 --> 00:45:59.130
and Kara's son Danny Strode are captured.

00:45:59.130 --> 00:46:00.380
We have to do a little bit of guesswork

00:46:00.380 --> 00:46:02.520
to figure out what the
cult's overall plan here is,

00:46:02.520 --> 00:46:04.210
but I think the plan is to kill the baby,

00:46:04.210 --> 00:46:06.480
which would effectively lift
the Curse of Thorn from Michael

00:46:06.480 --> 00:46:08.342
and give them the opportunity
to place it on Danny.

00:46:08.342 --> 00:46:09.360
That would explain

00:46:09.360 --> 00:46:11.100
why he's been hearing
the voices in his head,

00:46:11.100 --> 00:46:12.710
just like the six-year old Michael did

00:46:12.710 --> 00:46:14.770
the evening before he was
possessed to kill Judith.

00:46:14.770 --> 00:46:16.880
Michael's quiet yet destructive demeanor

00:46:16.880 --> 00:46:19.950
has surprised many of his
60+ victims over the years,

00:46:19.950 --> 00:46:22.720
but what he does next is a
different kind of surprise.

00:46:22.720 --> 00:46:25.580
Michael turns against the Cult of Thorn.

00:46:25.580 --> 00:46:27.615
(bloodcurdling scream)

00:46:27.615 --> 00:46:30.500
- He walks amongst us brother.

00:46:30.500 --> 00:46:31.870
He's come back.

00:46:31.870 --> 00:46:35.360
And he's very angry.

00:46:35.360 --> 00:46:37.410
- [Zac] Tommy and Kara have
one close encounter with him

00:46:37.410 --> 00:46:38.920
and then he just walks into the lab

00:46:38.920 --> 00:46:41.360
and starts cutting down
doctors, nurses and surgeons

00:46:41.360 --> 00:46:42.193
left and right.

00:46:42.193 --> 00:46:43.690
If you work in medicine in Haddonfield,

00:46:43.690 --> 00:46:45.850
just take the day off
on Halloween, seriously.

00:46:45.850 --> 00:46:46.800
We're left yet again

00:46:46.800 --> 00:46:49.480
to wonder why Michael's
behaviour changes so suddenly.

00:46:49.480 --> 00:46:50.340
I've seen it suggested

00:46:50.340 --> 00:46:52.430
that he was just tired
of obeying the cult.

00:46:52.430 --> 00:46:54.000
I think that makes no sense,

00:46:54.000 --> 00:46:54.890
why would he turn on them

00:46:54.890 --> 00:46:57.010
when he was potentially so
close to breaking the curse

00:46:57.010 --> 00:46:58.260
after 32 years?

00:46:58.260 --> 00:47:00.570
I see it as more of a
caged bear situation.

00:47:00.570 --> 00:47:01.930
While Michael is possessed by Thorn,

00:47:01.930 --> 00:47:03.620
he's essentially like a wild animal.

00:47:03.620 --> 00:47:04.640
Anyone who gets too close

00:47:04.640 --> 00:47:07.120
is in danger of being killed
by him, that's just his nature,

00:47:07.120 --> 00:47:08.030
what he does.

00:47:08.030 --> 00:47:09.730
He doesn't have any real allegiances,

00:47:09.730 --> 00:47:10.950
but he does still have the goal

00:47:10.950 --> 00:47:12.520
of killing off his next of kin.

00:47:12.520 --> 00:47:14.766
I'm not saying that he's
incapable of thinking for himself,

00:47:14.766 --> 00:47:16.580
we see him sneak up on people

00:47:16.580 --> 00:47:18.415
and make reactionary decisions
throughout the series,

00:47:18.415 --> 00:47:20.650
I'm just saying if he
has the chance to kill,

00:47:20.650 --> 00:47:22.170
he's probably going to.

00:47:22.170 --> 00:47:23.110
During this massacre,

00:47:23.110 --> 00:47:24.800
one of the medics escapes
out into the hall,

00:47:24.800 --> 00:47:26.830
and that's when he sees
Tommy and Kara trying to flee

00:47:26.830 --> 00:47:28.150
with the two young kids.

00:47:28.150 --> 00:47:29.590
This is the first time in a while

00:47:29.590 --> 00:47:32.060
that Michael is really close
to completing his main task,

00:47:32.060 --> 00:47:33.350
that is, wiping out his bloodline,

00:47:33.350 --> 00:47:34.960
so we see him actually walking faster

00:47:34.960 --> 00:47:36.320
than he's ever walked before.

00:47:36.320 --> 00:47:37.520
Tommy closes up this gate

00:47:37.520 --> 00:47:39.690
in order to create a barrier
between them and Michael,

00:47:39.690 --> 00:47:42.120
which totally screws over
this medic for no reason.

00:47:42.120 --> 00:47:44.080
Michael bashes the
guy's face into the bars

00:47:44.080 --> 00:47:45.870
and then just knocks down the gate anyway.

00:47:45.870 --> 00:47:47.260
Having spent 15 years there,

00:47:47.260 --> 00:47:48.910
this is kind of like Michael's home turf,

00:47:48.910 --> 00:47:51.410
so he's able to take some kind
of shortcut to cut them off.

00:47:51.410 --> 00:47:53.730
They duck into a random lab
filled with human embryos

00:47:53.730 --> 00:47:54.932
or babies growing in tanks.

00:47:54.932 --> 00:47:56.780
Some think that this means Jamie

00:47:56.780 --> 00:47:59.060
was artificially
inseminated to have Stephen,

00:47:59.060 --> 00:48:01.670
others believe this was a setup
for a seventh Halloween film

00:48:01.670 --> 00:48:02.580
that never happened.

00:48:02.580 --> 00:48:04.970
I don't think either of
those makes that much sense

00:48:04.970 --> 00:48:07.360
because these embryos are
clearly growing into babies

00:48:07.360 --> 00:48:10.360
outside the body, this
isn't a typical IVF lab.

00:48:10.360 --> 00:48:11.950
And this lab scene was actually added

00:48:11.950 --> 00:48:14.290
for the Theatrical Cut after
the death of Donald Pleasance,

00:48:14.290 --> 00:48:15.123
who plays Loomis.

00:48:15.123 --> 00:48:16.352
It would have been an
excellent opportunity

00:48:16.352 --> 00:48:19.580
to tie up any loose
threads, not cast new ones.

00:48:19.580 --> 00:48:21.760
Feel free to share your
own interpretations though.

00:48:21.760 --> 00:48:23.950
Michael punches through the
door to get access to the lab,

00:48:23.950 --> 00:48:26.350
and Tommy seems to concede to
him and offers up the baby,

00:48:26.350 --> 00:48:28.730
but of course it's just an
empty bundle of blankets.

00:48:28.730 --> 00:48:30.390
Tommy stabs four syringes into him

00:48:30.390 --> 00:48:32.450
and then Kara hits him
with a pipe over and over.

00:48:32.450 --> 00:48:34.180
He pins her to a lab table and chokes her,

00:48:34.180 --> 00:48:36.100
but lets her go after Danny yells out

00:48:36.100 --> 00:48:37.500
and gives away his position.

00:48:37.500 --> 00:48:38.890
- [Danny] Leave her alone!

00:48:38.890 --> 00:48:40.950
- Michael realizes that Danny has the baby

00:48:40.950 --> 00:48:42.050
and attempts to seize him,

00:48:42.050 --> 00:48:43.670
but Tommy drugs him one last time,

00:48:43.670 --> 00:48:46.000
giving Kara and the kids a
chance to make a run for it.

00:48:46.000 --> 00:48:48.743
Then Tommy beats him up with
a pipe Dr. Loomis style.

00:48:54.330 --> 00:48:56.580
Yeah, he's a little too
proud of himself there.

00:48:56.580 --> 00:48:57.630
And believe it or not,

00:48:57.630 --> 00:48:59.020
that is the last we ever see

00:48:59.020 --> 00:49:01.400
of the original iteration
of Michael Myers.

00:49:01.400 --> 00:49:03.300
The Theatrical Cut ends
with the suggestion

00:49:03.300 --> 00:49:05.690
of some kind of confrontation
between Michael and Loomis,

00:49:05.690 --> 00:49:07.330
where Loomis managed to get his mask off,

00:49:07.330 --> 00:49:08.901
but judging by this sound,

00:49:08.901 --> 00:49:10.630
- [Loomis] Aaargh!

00:49:10.630 --> 00:49:11.550
- I am led to believe

00:49:11.550 --> 00:49:13.900
that Michael ultimately
got the upper hand.

00:49:13.900 --> 00:49:16.040
The original continuity
ended with a whimper

00:49:16.040 --> 00:49:17.630
in terms of box-office revenue.

00:49:17.630 --> 00:49:18.580
Four, five and six

00:49:18.580 --> 00:49:21.180
represent three of the four
lowest grossing Halloween movies

00:49:21.180 --> 00:49:22.520
as of 2021.

00:49:22.520 --> 00:49:23.640
I don't really care about that,

00:49:23.640 --> 00:49:24.850
but from a horror perspective,

00:49:24.850 --> 00:49:27.210
it makes sense why the series
was falling out of favor.

00:49:27.210 --> 00:49:28.490
The Cult of Thorn storyline

00:49:28.490 --> 00:49:30.750
gives an explanation to
Michael Myers's creepy

00:49:30.750 --> 00:49:32.150
and unpredictable behaviour,

00:49:32.150 --> 00:49:35.130
and in a way, that
demystifies the character.

00:49:35.130 --> 00:49:36.130
- For years I've been convinced

00:49:36.130 --> 00:49:37.490
that there must be some reason.

00:49:37.490 --> 00:49:39.800
Some method behind Michael's madness.

00:49:39.800 --> 00:49:42.130
- But at the same time, as
we've seen in this video,

00:49:42.130 --> 00:49:44.240
there is still a lot to speculate about.

00:49:44.240 --> 00:49:46.270
I think back to the
sheer look of confusion

00:49:46.270 --> 00:49:48.950
when Laurie removes
Michael's mask in 1978.

00:49:48.950 --> 00:49:52.133
Michael operates at his
highest potential when he,

00:49:52.133 --> 00:49:53.990
the mysteries of his character,
and his true intentions

00:49:53.990 --> 00:49:56.080
are properly masked.

00:49:56.080 --> 00:49:58.350
Click that playlist on the
left for my entire catalogue

00:49:58.350 --> 00:50:00.710
of Halloween franchise
Horror History episodes.

00:50:00.710 --> 00:50:02.810
If you love horror and
all things Halloween,

00:50:02.810 --> 00:50:04.560
remember to subscribe to CZsWorld

00:50:04.560 --> 00:50:05.930
for new horrors every week,

00:50:05.930 --> 00:50:08.001
ring the deathbell and
select all notifications

00:50:08.001 --> 00:50:10.450
and I will see you in the next one.

00:50:10.450 --> 00:50:12.343
Assuming the planets align.

00:50:12.343 --> 00:50:14.926
(upbeat music)

